hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7801","7801 - Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Qahir ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing the ant and the bee and the shrike and the hoopoe, and sometimes he was silent about the fourth. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, except Sulayman ibn Abi Sulayman, nor do we know it narrated from Abu Hurayra except from this angle, and he was contradicted in its isnad. Ibn Jurayj narrated it, from al-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Ibn Abbas. And others narrated it from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Ibn Abbas. And Ibn Jurayj's hadith is the best narrated in that, and I think Sulayman ibn Arqam, and he is weak in hadith."
"7802","7802 - Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Qahir narrated to us, he said: Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said about the slain of Uhud: Shroud them with their wounds and blood. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayra except from this angle with this isnad, and we already mentioned Sulayman with weakness, though the trustworthy narrated this hadith from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from Jabir, and a man not strong narrated it, from al-Zuhri, from Ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, from his father."
"7803","7803 - And Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Asid al-Bahili narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn al-Awwam narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A leg is without liability. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, except Sufyan ibn Husayn."
"7804","7804 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Arqam, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever cups on Wednesday or Saturday and vitiligo befalls him, let him blame only himself. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this angle, and Sulayman ibn Arqam is weak in hadith, and it only came from him."
"7805","7805 - And Yahya ibn al-Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Junada ibn Muhammad al-Dimashqi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Habib ibn Abi al-Ishrin narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will surely be selected as dates are selected from refuse, and your best will go, and your worst will remain, so die if you can. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayra, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except from this angle with this isnad, and Abd al-Hamid is not bad."
"7806","7806 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no fara' and no atira."
"7807","7807 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Rawh narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until you fight a people whose shoes are hair, as if their faces are hammered shields. And this hadith more than one narrated from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, among them Ibn Uyayna."
"7808","7808 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a funeral, and stood to pray over it, and they said: He has a debt. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take your companion and pray over him. A man said: His debt is upon me, so pray over him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and prayed over him. And this hadith Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salama, and we do not know anyone who said: from Sa'id, except Ibn Abi Hafsah."
"7809","7809 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, exalted, laughs at two men, one of them kills the other, then admits them both to Paradise. It was said: How is that? He said: One of them is a disbeliever and kills the other, then embraces Islam and is killed."
"7810","7810 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: In this black seed is healing from every disease except death. It was said: What is death? He said: Death. And this hadith Ibn Abi Hafsah and Yunus narrated, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, and Ibn Uyayna narrated it, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra."
"7811","7811 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Arqam narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever cups on Saturday and Wednesday and vitiligo befalls him, let him blame only himself. And this hadith others besides Sulayman narrated, from al-Zuhri, mursal, and Sulayman is weak in hadith."
"7812","7812 - Safwan ibn al-Mughallis narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatada, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers in others except the Sacred Mosque. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Qatada, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, except Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata, from Sa'id."
"7813","7813 - Nasr ibn Ali and Amr ibn Ali and Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, and the wording is Nasr's. He said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham informed us, from his father, from Qatada, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A prophet among the prophets raided after Asr and said: No man who built a house and did not live in it shall accompany me, or married a woman and did not consummate with her. He said: And nothing remained of the sun except a little, and he said: O Allah, the sun is commanded and I am commanded, O Allah, hold it. So Allah held it an hour until Allah gave him victory, and he ordered the spoils and they were gathered, and fire came and did not eat them, and he said: Among you is misappropriation, so from every tribe let a man come and pledge to me. So his hand stuck to the hand of a man or two men, and he said: Among you is misappropriation! So they brought out a cow's head of gold and cast it into the spoils, and it, meaning the fire, ate it. The Messenger of Allah said: Spoils were not lawful for anyone before us, and that is because Allah, blessed and exalted, saw our weakness, so He made them good for us. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Qatada, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, except Mu'adh ibn Hisham, from his father."
"7814","7814 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Bazi' narrated to us, he said: Abu Bahr Abd al-Rahman ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Aruba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The price of the cat was forbidden."
"7815","7815 - Ahmad ibn Abdullah al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham and Imran narrated to us, from Qatada, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in two wraps and a Najrani cloak. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Qatada, from Ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, joined, except Abu Dawud, and more than one narrated it, among them Yazid ibn Zuray' and others, from Hisham, from Qatada, from Ibn al-Musayyib, mursal."
"7816","7816 - Amr ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Bayan narrated to us, he said: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatada, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, he said: We were in a company with Umar, and he said: Who narrates to us? The wind blew and I was at the end of the people, and Umar said: Which of you heard something from the Messenger of Allah about wind? I said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Wind is from Allah's mercy, it comes with mercy and punishment, so when you see it, ask Allah for its good and seek refuge with Allah from its evil, and do not revile it, for it is commanded."
"7817","7817 - Muhammad ibn Rizqullah al-Kalwadhani narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Abu Hilal narrated to us, from Qatada, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When two caliphs are pledged, kill the latter of them. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Qatada, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, except Abu Hilal, and others besides Abu Hilal narrated it mursal."
"7818","7818 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd and Qatada, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, blessed and exalted, said: Pride is My cloak, and greatness is My lower garment, so whoever disputes with Me one of them, I cast him, or he said: I throw him into the Fire. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Qatada, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, except Hammad ibn Salama, nor from Hammad except Sahl."
"7819","7819 - Rizq ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Qatada, from Sa'id and al-Hasan and Ata, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The thief does not steal while he steals and he is a believer, nor commits zina while he commits zina and he is a believer, nor drinks wine while he drinks it and he is a believer. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Qatada except al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik alone."
"7820","7820 - Abu Bakr ibn Nafi' narrated to us, he said: Mas'ud ibn Wasil narrated to us, he said: al-Nahhas ibn Qahm narrated to us, from Qatada, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: There are no days in which deeds are better than the ten days, meaning the ten of Dhu al-Hijja; fasting a day of them equals fasting a year, and standing a night of them equals standing the Night of Decree, so increase tasbih and takbir and remembrance of Allah. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Qatada except al-Nahhas ibn Qahm, and he is a man from Basra, there is no harm in him, and none narrated it from him except Mas'ud ibn Wasil, and he is a Basran man, there is no harm in him."
"7821","7821 - And I heard Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari mentioning from Muhammad ibn Bakkar ibn Bilal, from Sa'id ibn Bashir, from Qatada, from Ibn al-Musayyib and Abi al-Aliya, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade marrying a woman over her paternal aunt and over her maternal aunt. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Qatada, from Ibn al-Musayyib and Abi al-Aliya, from Abu Hurayra, except Sa'id ibn Bashir."
"7822","7822 - And I heard Muhammad ibn Sa'id ibn Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari mentioning from Abu Asim, from Hammam, from Qatada, from Sa'id, and from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: A woman is not married over her paternal aunt, nor over her maternal aunt. And this hadith, the raised part in my view is the hadith of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, and the hadith of Sa'id is mursal, and both were joined in this hadith."
"7823","7823 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham informed us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Qatada, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a prophet among the prophets raided with his companions and said: No man who built a house and did not live in it shall accompany me, or married a woman and did not enter with her, or has a need to return. He met the enemy at sunset and said: O Allah, it is commanded and I am commanded, so hold it for me until You judge between me and them. So Allah held it for him and he conquered. The spoils were placed and fire did not eat them, and they, when they gained spoils, fire was sent upon them and ate them. Their prophet said to them: You misappropriated, so from every tribe of you let a man come to me and pledge to me. So they pledged him, and the hand of a man of them stuck to his hand. He said: Gather your companions, they misappropriated, so bring them to me to pledge me. So they came to him, and his hand stuck to the hand of two men of them. He said: You misappropriated. They said: Yes, we misappropriated the image of a cow, meaning: a cow's horn of gold. He said: He brought it and cast it into the spoils, and fire was sent upon it and ate it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, fed us the spoils as mercy He had mercy on us with, for what He knows of our weakness. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Qatada, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, except Mu'adh ibn Hisham, from his father."
"7824","7824 - Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id. Ibrahim ibn Hani and Ahmad ibn al-Husayn ibn Abbad Abu al-Abbas narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Sinan al-Ruhawi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nuh had Sam, Ham and Yafith born to him. To Sam were born Arabs, Persians and Romans, and good is in them. To Yafith were born Gog and Magog, Turks and Slavs, and no good is in them. To Ham were born Copts, Berbers and Sudanese. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Abu Hurayra with this isnad, nor do we know anyone narrated it musnad from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, except Yazid ibn Sinan, nor from Yazid except his son. A group of scholars narrated from him and accepted his hadith. Others narrated it from Yahya ibn Sa'id mursal, and did not narrate it musnad, only making it from Sa'id's saying."
"7825","7825 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari and Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us, they said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, from his brother Abu Bakr, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Satan ties three knots on the back of the head of one of you when he sleeps. If he wakes and remembers Allah, a knot is untied. If he stands and performs ablution, a knot is untied. If he stands and prays, all his knots are untied. He wakes lively, good in soul. And if he wakes and does not do that, he wakes lazy, evil in soul, not attaining good."
"7826","7826 - Muhammad ibn Isma'il and Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us, and the wording is Muhammad ibn Isa's, they said: Ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, from his brother, from Sulayman, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I saw Amr ibn Luhayy dragging his intestines in the Fire. And these two hadiths, we do not know anyone narrated them from Yahya, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, except Sulayman ibn Bilal, nor do we know anyone narrated them from Sulayman except Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways, and they are known from Abu Hurayra's hadith, that narrated from Abu Hurayra by paths."
"7827","7827 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Ata ibn al-Agharr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over the Negus. And this hadith Zam'a narrated from al-Zuhri and Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we do not know it narrated from Yahya, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, except from these two paths."
"7828","7828 - Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr al-Humaydi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra, he said: He forbade marrying a woman over her paternal aunt and over her maternal aunt. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Yahya, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, except Sufyan. Al-Humaydi and Abu Muslim al-Mustamli narrated it from Sufyan."
"7829","7829 - Muhammad ibn Mirdas narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Umar al-Qaysi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no commander of ten except he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hand chained to his neck. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Yahya ibn Sa'id except Ubayd, and the trustworthy narrate it from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, and that is correct."
"7830","7830 - Salih ibn Mu'adh Abu Bishr narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sirma narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was favored over the prophets with two traits; my devil was a disbeliever, so Allah aided me over him until he submitted, and I forgot the other trait. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, except Ibrahim ibn Sirma, and he is not strong in hadith."
"7831","7827 - Al-Abbas ibn Jafar, he being Ibn Abi Talib al-Baghdadi, narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Mumin ibn Abbad narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Muhammad al-Nasai narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not from us who corrupts a woman against her husband, or a slave against his master. And this hadith we do not know from the hadith of Yahya ibn Said, from Abu Hurayrah, except through this route, and Abd al-Mumin ibn Abbad and Harun ibn Muhammad are not well known for transmission, and we only mentioned this hadith with the defect in it to clarify that this man alone narrated it."
"7832","7828 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Ibrahim circumcised himself with a qadum (an adze/axe-like tool) - I think he said - when eighty years had passed over him. And this hadith a group narrated from Yahya ibn Said, from Abu Hurayrah, as mawquf (stopped at the Companion), and al-Awzai attributed it (in marfu form) from Yahya; al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated it from al-Awzai, from Yahya ibn Said, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7833","7829 - Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Yahya ibn Said, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, as far as I know, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Treat goats well, and remove harm from them, for they are among the riding animals of Paradise. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from al-Zuhri, from Yahya ibn Said, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, except Said ibn Muhammad, and he was not corroborated in this hadith."
"7834","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Said. 7830 - Muhammad ibn al-Hasan, known as Ibn Abi Ali al-Kirmani, informed us, he said: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Said ibn al-Musayyib and al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you prays over the funeral, let him be sincere in supplication for it."
"7835","Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Said. 7831 - Safwan ibn Mughallis narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Asbahani, meaning Muhammad ibn Said, narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Abu Ayyub al-Ifriqi, he being Muhammad ibn Said ibn al-Asbahani, narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come peoples who will lead you in prayer; if they complete it, it is for them and for you, and if they do not complete it, it is upon them and for you. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, except Safwan, and none narrated it from Safwan except Abu Ayyub, and from Abu Ayyub narrated Abd al-Rahim and Ibn Abi Zaidah, and Safwan attributed (in marfu form) from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, no hadith other than this one."
"7836","Bukayr ibn Abd Allah, from Said. 7832 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the atirah, and it was a sacrifice they used to slaughter in Rajab, so he forbade them from it, and commanded them with the udhiyah (sacrificial animal). And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Abu Hurayrah except Said, nor from Said except Bukayr, nor from Bukayr except Ibn Lahiah, and we do not know that Bukayr attributed (in marfu form) from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, except this hadith."
"7837","Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Said. 7833 - Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Hayyaj narrated to us, he said: Abu Nuaym narrated to us, he said: Abd Allah ibn Amir al-Aslami narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib: that Umar passed by Hassan ibn Thabit while he was reciting poetry in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Do you recite poetry in the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I recited before one who is better than you. So Abu Hurayrah said: He spoke the truth. This hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Ibn Harmalah except Abd Allah ibn Amir, and he is not strong, and al-Zuhri narrated it from Said, from Abu Hurayrah."
"7838","7834 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Abi al-Hunayn narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Asamm narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Zinad narrated to us, from Ibn Harmalah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan concerns himself with one and with two, but when they are three he does not concern himself with them."
"7839","7834 (m) - And also Muhammad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will remain in good as long as they hasten the breaking of the fast, and do not delay it with the delaying of the people of shirk (polytheism). And the two hadiths of Ibn Harmalah we do not know anyone narrated except Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad, and he heard them only from Ibn Abi al-Hunayn, from Abd al-Aziz. And the first hadith, 'Satan concerns himself with one,' was narrated by others than Ibn Abi al-Zinad, from Ibn Harmalah, from Umar, and Ibn Shuayb from his father, from his grandfather. Abu Jabir al-Bayadi, from Said."
"7840","7836 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Habban ibn Hilal narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Abu Jabir al-Bayadi, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever catches one rakah of Friday prayer, let him add another to it. And we do not know that Abu Jabir attributed (in marfu form) from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, except this hadith, nor did anyone narrate it from him except al-Hajjaj, nor from al-Hajjaj except Abd al-Wahid ibn Ziyad, and we heard it only from Muhammad ibn Mamar, from Habban. And Abu Jabir is a man from the people of Madinah, his name is Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman; Ibn Abi Dhib narrated from him; he is salih al-hadith (acceptable in hadith). Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Said."
"7841","7837 - Yahya ibn Mualla ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Salt narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast three days from every month. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, except Ibn Aqil, nor did anyone narrate it from Ibn Aqil except Amr ibn Thabit. And Ibn Aqil - al-Thawri and Zaidah and a large group narrated from him - and Amr ibn Thabit, the people accepted his hadith."
"7842","Muslim ibn Yannaq, from Said. 7838 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Yunus ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Yannaq, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: My close friend enjoined upon me three things: fasting three days from every month, the two rakahs of Duha, and that I not sleep except upon witr."
"7843","Amr ibn Dinar, from Said. 7839 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qatii narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakr, he being al-Bursani, narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Yazid, he being al-Khuzi, narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast."
"7844","7840 - And Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bazi narrated it to us with it, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: al-Muthanna narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast."
"7845","Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Said. 7841 - Yahya ibn Khalaf, he being al-Bahili, narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala - he is Ibn Abd al-Ala al-Basri - narrated to us, he said: Dawud narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by twenty-five prayers."
"7846","7842 - And Yahya ibn al-Mualla narrated it to us with it, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Muadh narrated to us, from his father, from Ashath, from Dawud, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. And we do not know that Ashath attributed (in marfu form) from Dawud anything other than this hadith, and Dawud did not attribute from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, except two hadiths, this being one of them, and the other is:"
"7847","7843 - Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad, he being Ibn Nasr al-Bahili, narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Dawud, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three traits, whoever has them in him is a hypocrite, even if he fasts and prays and claims he is a believer: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks it, and when he is entrusted he betrays. And this hadith none narrated from Dawud, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"7848","Ali ibn Zayd, he being Ibn Judan, from Said. 7844 - Muhammad ibn Mamar, he being al-Bahrani, and Abu Hurayrah Muhammad ibn Firas narrated to us, they said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The height of Adam was sixty cubits, with seven cubits in width."
"7849","7845 - Raja ibn Muhammad al-Saqati narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head after he had given the salutation while facing the qiblah, and said: O Allah, deliver Salamah ibn Hisham, and Ayyash ibn Abi Rabiah, and al-Walid ibn al-Walid, and the weak Muslims who can find no stratagem nor are guided to a way. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, except Abd al-Warith."
"7850","7846 - Raja ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your Lord - blessed and exalted - says: Every good deed is for ten of its likes up to seven hundredfold, and fasting is Mine and I reward for it, and fasting is a shield from the Fire, and the breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk. Abu Bakr said: I think Imran ibn Musa narrated it to us with it, from Abd al-Warith himself, with this chain. And we do not know anyone narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, except Abd al-Warith."
"7851","7847 - Muhammad ibn Abi Ghalib and Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mualla al-Adami narrated to us, they said: Uthman ibn Said ibn Murrah narrated to us, he said: al-Minhal ibn Khalifah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no person except that in his head is a bridle (hikmah), and the bridle is in the hand of an angel; if he is humble it is said to the angel: raise the bridle, and if he seeks to rise high it is said to the angel: put down his bridle. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, except al-Minhal ibn Khalifah."
"7852","7848 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd and Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in what he narrates from his Lord, blessed and exalted, He said: Pride is My cloak and greatness is My lower garment; whoever contends with Me for one of them, I will throw him down or cast him into the Fire. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Ali ibn Zayd except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"7853","7849 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qutai narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Said, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The last two men to come out of the Fire: Allah, blessed and exalted, says to one of them: O son of Adam, what did you prepare for this Day? Did you ever do any good? Did you hope in Me or fear Me? He says: No, my Lord. So he is commanded to the Fire, and he is the most regretful of the people of the Fire. And He says to the other: O son of Adam, what did you prepare for this Day? Did you do any good? He says: No, except that I used to hope in You. Then a tree is raised for him, and he says: My Lord, seat me under this tree, so I may shade in its shade, eat from its fruit, and drink from its water, and he covenants with Him not to ask Him for other than it. So he sits, or He seats him, under it. Then another tree is raised for him, better than the first, and he says: My Lord, bring me near to this tree - I will not ask You for other than it - to shade in its shade and drink from its water. He says: O son of Adam, did you not covenant with Me not to ask Me for other than it? He says: Yes, my Lord, but this one. And he covenants with Him not to ask Him for other than it, so He brings him near to it. Then a tree is raised for him at the gate of Paradise, better than the first two, and he says: Bring me near under this one, and he covenants with Him not to ask Him for other than it, so He brings him near to it. Then he hears the voices of the people of Paradise and cannot restrain himself, so he says: My Lord, admit me to Paradise - I think he said: so he enters Paradise - and Allah, blessed and exalted, says: Ask and wish. So he asks and wishes for the span of three days - I think he said: of the days of this world - and he wishes, and when he finishes He says: Yours is what you asked. Abu Hurayrah said: and the like of it with him. Abu Said said: and ten times its like with him. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said, except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"7854","7850 - Muhammad ibn al-Aswad al-Ammi narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd al-Samad Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Miqdam narrated to us, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: We have seen everything the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told us, except that he said: Men to whom it will be said on the Day of Resurrection: Put down your whips and enter the Fire. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, except Abu al-Miqdam, he being Hisham ibn Ziyad, he is not strong, and we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayrah through other than this route."
"7855","7851 - Umar ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Amr al-Qaysi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The head of intellect after faith in Allah is showing affection to people. And this hadith Hushaym narrated from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, as mursal, and Ubayd ibn Amr is not a preserver (of hadith), especially when he contradicts the trustworthy narrators."
"7856","7852 - al-Fadl ibn Yaqub al-Jazari narrated to us, he said: Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from al-Ahwas ibn Hakim, from Abu Awn, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: When revelation descended upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he would suffer headache, so he would wrap his head with henna. And this hadith we do not know narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this route with this chain, and we do not know that Abu Awn attributed (in marfu form) from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, any hadith other than this one. The second part of the hadith of Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, is complete."
"7857","Al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah. 7853 - Abu Abd Allah Muhammad ibn Attab narrated to us, he said: Abu Ayyub Sulayman ibn Khalaf, known as Ibn Nufayl, narrated to us, he said: Abu Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us, he said: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Satan comes to one of you and confuses him in his prayer, until he does not know how much he prayed. So whoever of you finds any of that, let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting."
"7858","7854 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah has not permitted anything as He has permitted a prophet to chant the Quran. Sufyan said: to be sufficed by it (to regard it as sufficient)."
"7859","7855 - And Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: that al-Aqra ibn Habis saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was kissing al-Hasan, and he said: I have ten children, I never kissed one of them. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy. This hadith was narrated by more than one from al-Zuhri, among them Ibn Uyaynah and Hushaym and others."
"7860","7856 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: In the black seed there is healing from every disease except death. This hadith was narrated from al-Zuhri, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah, and Ibn Uyaynah said: from Abu Salamah."
"7861","7857 - And Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever catches one rakah of the prayer has caught it."
"7862","7858 - And Abd Allah ibn Said narrated it to us with it, he said: Abd Allah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever catches one rakah of the prayer has caught it."
"7863","7859 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever catches one rakah of the prayer has caught it."
"7864","7860 - And Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you wakes from his sleep, let him not dip his hand into the vessel until he washes it, for he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"7865","7861 - And Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever stands Ramadan in faith and seeking reward, his past sins are forgiven."
"7866","7862 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The grazing animal (that causes harm) is without liability, the mine is without liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"7867","7863 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, from Malik, from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The wound of the grazing animal is without liability, the mine is without liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"7868","7864 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed me, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he forbade making nabidh in dubba (gourd) and muzaffat (pitched vessel). He said: And avoid hantam (green jars) and naqir (hollowed stumps)."
"7869","7865 - And Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed me, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"7870","7866 - And Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: When al-Najashi died, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek forgiveness for him."
"7871","7867 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The child belongs to the bed, and for the adulterer is the stone."
"7872","7868 - And Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: that he used to say takbir whenever he lowered and raised, and he would say: I am the most like you in the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7873","7869 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I am the most like you in the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he used to say takbir whenever he lowered and raised."
"7874","7870 - And Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Tasbih is for men, and clapping is for women."
"7875","7871 - And Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, with the like of it."
"7876","7872 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: that two women, one of them threw at the other, causing her to miscarry a fetus, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged for the fetus a male slave or a female child."
"7877","7873 - And Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed me, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Two women of Hudhayl fought, and one of them threw a stone at the other, striking her belly, killing her and causing her to abort her fetus. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged her blood money upon the aqilah (male relatives) of the other, and for the fetus a ghurrah, a male slave or a female slave. Then a speaker said: Do we pay blood money for one who neither ate nor drank, nor looked nor cried so as to raise his voice? Such as that is wasted. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is from the brothers of the soothsayers. And this hadith was narrated from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah; Yunus and others narrated it."
"7878","7874 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood at al-Hazwarah and said: I know that you are the most beloved land of Allah to Him, meaning Makkah, and were it not that my people expelled me from you, I would not have left. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, except Mamar."
"7879","7875 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The poor person is not the one whom one or two dates turn away, nor one or two morsels. They said: Then who is the poor person? He said: The one who finds no sufficiency, and whose place is not known so that charity may be given to him. Al-Zuhri said: And that is the deprived one."
"7880","7876 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contagion, no hamah, and no safar. Then a Bedouin said: O Messenger of Allah, what about camels like gazelles, then a mangy camel mixes with them and they all become mangy? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then who infected the first?"
"7881","7877 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Do not say 'the failure of time,' for Allah is time. And this hadith was narrated by more than one from al-Zuhri, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah."
"7882","7878 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the servant of one of you prepares food, let him seat him with him; if he refuses, let him hand him his food in his hand."
"7883","7879 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When you see it, fast, and when you see it, break the fast; if it is obscured for you, then fast thirty days. And this hadith was narrated by Ibrahim ibn Sad, from al-Zuhri, from Said, from Abu Hurayrah."
"7884","7880 - Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade wisal (continuous fasting). They said: O Messenger of Allah, you practice wisal! He said: My Lord, blessed and exalted, feeds me and gives me drink. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continued fasting with them for two days and two nights, then he saw the crescent. And this hadith was narrated from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah."
"7885","7881 - And Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The prayer was established, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and stood in his place of prayer, then he remembered that he had not performed ghusl, so he left and said: Stay as you are - and we formed rows - then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came with his head dripping and led us in prayer."
"7886","7882 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, descends to the lowest heaven when a third of the night remains, and says: Who calls upon Me that I may answer him? Who seeks My forgiveness that I may forgive him? Who asks that I may give him - or he said: Who asks Me that I may give him. And this hadith was narrated from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah and al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah. More than one narrated it, and Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated it from al-Zuhri, from al-Agharr and Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Hurayrah."
"7887","7883 - And Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: You find people as mines; the best of them in ignorance are the best of them in Islam."
"7888","7884 - And Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed me, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah, and whoever obeys my commander has obeyed me, and whoever disobeys my commander has disobeyed me."
"7889","7885 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"7890","7886 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses, in their forelocks is good until the Day of Resurrection. And this hadith we do not know from the hadith of al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, except from the hadith of Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar."
"7891","7887 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed me, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, does one of us pray in a single garment? He said: Do all of you find two garments?!"
"7892","7888 - And Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Adam and Musa argued. Musa said: O Adam, you are the one who admitted your offspring into the Fire. So Adam said - as I think - for how much do you find that against me? Meaning: written - He said: So Adam overcame Musa. And this hadith was differed upon from al-Zuhri: al-Zuhri narrated it from Abu Salamah, and al-Zuhri narrated it from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, and he narrated it from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj."
"7893","7889 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever keeps a dog, except a dog for livestock or hunting, a qirat is deducted from his reward every day."
"7894","7890 - Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah and Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Shall I not inform you of the best quarters of the Ansar? They said: Yes. He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Banu al-Najjar. They said: Then who? He said: Then Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj, then Banu Saidah. They said: Then who, O Messenger of Allah? He said: And in every quarter of the Ansar there is good. And this hadith was narrated by Abu al-Zinad and Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Usayd."
"7895","7891 - And Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah and Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7896","7892 - And Ahmad ibn Abdah and Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated it to us with it. Ahmad said: he informed us, and Khalid said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah and Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Jews and Christians do not dye, so differ from them."
"7897","7893 - And Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Zuhr and Asr and gave the salutation after two rakahs, then left. Then Dhu al-Shimalayn ibn Abd ibn Amr - he being an ally of Banu Zuhrah - said to him: O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened or did you forget? So the Messenger of Allah said: What does Dhu al-Yadayn say? They said: He spoke the truth - so he completed with them the two rakahs he had omitted. Al-Zuhri said: Then he prostrated two prostrations after he finished. Al-Zuhri said: And that was before, then matters were perfected afterward. And this hadith was narrated by Yunus from al-Zuhri, from Said and Abu Salamah and Ubayd Allah, from Abu Hurayrah. And al-Awzai also narrated it, and al-Zuhri narrated it from Ibn Abi Hathmah, from Abu Hurayrah. And al-Zuhri narrated it from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah; all of these narrated it."
"7898","7894 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever keeps a dog, except a dog for livestock or hunting, a qirat is deducted from his reward every day."
"7899","7895 - And Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not harm his neighbor, and whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent."
"7900","7896 - Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Hour will not come until two groups fight, their claim being one."
"7901","7897 - And Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Shuayb narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Fire complained to its Lord and said: Parts of me have consumed parts of me. So He permitted for it two breaths: a breath in the winter and a breath in the summer, and it is the most intense heat you find and the most intense cold (zamharir) you find."
"7902","7898 - Raja ibn Muhammad al-Saqati narrated to us, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: al-Awzai narrated to us, from Qurrah, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Every important matter not begun with praise is cut off. And this hadith we do not know narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this route with this chain."
"7903","7899 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Qurrah, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Allah, blessed and exalted, said: The most beloved of My servants to Me are those quickest to break the fast."
"7904","7900 - Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Qurrah, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When the reciter says amin, then say amin."
"7905","7901 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Juwayriyah narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a young man, and I fear hardship for myself, and I do not find the means to marry women, so do you command me to castrate myself? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The pen has run upon what is decreed; castrate yourself if you wish, or leave it. And this hadith we do not know narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this route with this chain."
"7906","7902 - Ismail ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Our lodging tomorrow, if Allah wills, is at Khayf of Banu Kinanah, where they swore upon disbelief."
"7907","7903 - And Abu Musa narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Juwayriyah narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"7908","7904 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Yamar ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Ibn al-Mubarak, from al-Awzai, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no ruler except that he has two confidants: a confidant commanding him to good and forbidding him from evil, and a confidant sparing him no corruption. So whoever is shielded from the evil of the latter is shielded. And this hadith was differed upon: Yunus narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Said, and al-Awzai said: from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, and Muhammad ibn Amr narrated it from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, and Safwan ibn Sulaym narrated it from Abu Salamah, from Abu Ayyub."
"7909","7905 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Shortening the salutation is sunnah. And this hadith was narrated by others than Ibn al-Mubarak, from al-Awzai, from Qurrah, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah."
"7910","7906 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from al-Numan, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw Abd Allah ibn Hudhafah pray and raise his voice in recitation, so he said: O Abd Allah, do not make me hear, and make Allah hear."
"7911","7907 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the recitation of Abd Allah ibn Qays and said: He has been given a flute from the flutes of the family of Dawud. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, except Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah."
"7912","7908 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sufyan narrated to us, he said: Salih narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Woman is like a rib; if you strive to straighten it you break it, and if you enjoy it you enjoy it while there is crookedness in it."
"7913","7909 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I am closer to every believer than his own self; whoever leaves wealth, it is for his heirs, and whoever leaves debt, it is upon me."
"7914","7910 - Abd Allah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Yaqub narrated to us, from Umar ibn Said, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: None endures its hardship except that I am a witness for him on the Day of Resurrection."
"7915","7911 - Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Rawh narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Hafsah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Journey is only to three mosques: the Sacred Mosque, the mosque of Madinah, and the mosque of Iliya (Jerusalem)."
"7916","7912 - Ahmad ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Jahm informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Imru al-Qays is the leader of the poets toward the Fire. And this hadith we do not know narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this route with this chain."
"7917","7913 - Abd Allah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: I found in my father's book, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dignity and tranquility are among the people of sheep, and pride and arrogance are among the people of camels, from the people of Najd. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith is Yemeni, and wisdom is Yemeni."
"7918","7914 - al-Abbas ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from Uqayl, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when he was concerned he would frequently touch his beard. And this hadith we do not know narrated from Abu Hurayrah except through this route with this chain."
"7919","Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah. 7915 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A Bedouin entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in the mosque, and said: O Allah, forgive me and Muhammad, and forgive no one with us. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have confined what is vast. He said: Then the Bedouin turned away until he came to a side of the mosque and urinated in it, and he was not rebuked nor insulted. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This mosque was built only for the remembrance of Allah and prayer. Then he called for a bucket of water and poured it over it."
"7920","7916 - And Usayd ibn Asim narrated it to us, he said: Salih ibn Mihran narrated to us, he said: al-Numan ibn Abd al-Salam narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it. And we do not know anyone narrated this hadith from Sufyan except al-Numan."
"7921","7917 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cool down from the prayer, for the intensity of heat is from the blast of Hell."
"7922","7918 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about prayer in a single garment. He said: Do all of you find two garments?"
"7923","7919 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The excellence of congregational prayer over the prayer of the solitary is twenty-five degrees."
"7924","7920 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until the Euphrates recedes from a mountain of gold, and people fight over it, and nine hundred out of every thousand are killed."
"7925","7921 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every predator with fangs, and the mu jaththamah (animal used as a target), and the domestic donkey, on the day of Khaybar."
"7926","7922 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In the black seed there is healing from every disease except death. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is death? He said: Death is death."
"7927","7923 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves the Ansar, Allah loves him, and whoever hates the Ansar, Allah hates him."
"7928","7924 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I seek Allah's forgiveness one hundred times every day."
"7929","7925 - And Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, said: I am al-Rahman and it is the womb (rahim); I derived for it from My name. So whoever joins it, I join him, and whoever cuts it, I cut him off. And this hadith we know only from Muhammad ibn Bashshar, from Abd al-Wahhab, and al-Zuhri narrated it from Abu Salamah, from Abu Raddad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf."
"7930","7926 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and saw a palace. I said: Whose is this? It was said: Umar's. Nothing kept me from entering it except what I knew of your jealousy, O Umar! He said: Then Umar wept and said: Would I be jealous of you, O Messenger of Allah?"
"7931","7927 - Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"7932","7928 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he raised it (to the Prophet), he said: Charity is only from surplus wealth, and the upper hand is better than the lower hand, and begin with those you support."
"7933","7929 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My pulpit is upon a rivulet from the rivulets of Paradise."
"7934","7930 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The orphan girl is consulted about herself; if she is silent, that is her permission, and if she refuses, there is no compulsion upon her."
"7935","7931 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The poor believers enter Paradise before the rich by half a day of the days of the Hereafter, amounting to five hundred years."
"7936","7932 - Abd al-Ala ibn Wasil narrated it to us with it, he said: Thabit ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Sufyan, meaning al-Thawri, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"7937","7933 - Abd al-Ala ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Khallad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"7938","7934 - And Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The noble, son of the noble, son of the noble is Yusuf ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I remained in prison as long as Yusuf remained, then the caller came to me, I would have answered. And he said: May Allah have mercy on Lut; he used to take refuge in a strong support, when he said to his people: If only I had strength against you, or refuge in a strong support. He said: No prophet was sent after him except that he was sent among the affluent of his people."
"7939","7935 - And Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever catches one rakah of the Fajr prayer before the sun rises has caught it, and whoever catches - Muhammad said: I doubt - one rakah or two rakahs of Asr before the sun sets has caught it."
"7940","7936 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sees me in a dream has seen the truth, for Satan does not resemble me."
"7941","7937 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood in the year of the Conquest at al-Hajun and said: By Allah, you are the best land of Allah and the most beloved land of Allah to Allah, and were I not expelled from you I would not have left. And it was not lawful for anyone before me, nor is it lawful for anyone after me, and it was made lawful for me only for an hour of the day, then it is sacred at this hour of mine: its trees are not cut, its grass is not gathered, and its lost item is not picked up except for one who announces it. He said: Then a man said - he said, and the people claimed he was Abbas - O Messenger of Allah, except idhkhir (a fragrant grass), for it is for our houses, our graves, and our furnaces. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Except idhkhir."
"7942","7938 - And Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to me, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: that a man of the Ansar heard a man of the Jews say: By the One who chose Musa above mankind, so he raised his hand and slapped him. Then he brought him to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. The Ansari said: He said: By the One who chose Musa above mankind, while you are among us. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Trumpet is blown, and whoever is in the heavens and whoever is on earth falls unconscious except whom Allah wills. Then it is blown in another time, and I am the first to raise his head, and behold Musa holding onto a leg of the Throne's legs. I do not know whether he was among those Allah exempted, or he raised his head before me. And whoever says: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta has lied."
"7943","7939 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ibrahim, peace be upon him, circumcised himself at the age of eighty years, with a qadum."
"7944","7940 - And Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: that a funeral passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they praised it with good among the traits of good. He said: It is due. Then another passed by him, and they praised it with evil among the traits of evil. He said: It is due. Then he said: You are the witnesses of Allah on earth."
"7945","7941 - And Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The sick (camel owner) does not bring (his camels) upon the healthy."
"7946","7942 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Change the white hair, and do not resemble the Jews and Christians."
"7947","7943 - And Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ghifar and Aslam and whoever is of Juhaynah are better than the two allies: Ghatafan, Asad, Hawazin, and Tamim."
"7948","7944 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fire of Hell was made superior to this fire of yours by seventy-six parts, or ninety-six parts. They said: O Messenger of Allah, it would have sufficed."
"7949","7945 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The most complete of the believers in faith are the best of them in character."
"7950","7946 - al-Hasan ibn Qazaah narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Modesty is from faith, and faith is in Paradise, and obscenity is from harshness, and harshness is in the Fire."
"7951","7947 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The best of you are the best of you to their women."
"7952","7948 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Taymi narrated to us, they said: Quraysh ibn Anas narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you are the best of you to my wives after me. He said: So Abd al-Rahman bequeathed such-and-such to them, and it was sold for four hundred thousand. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Muhammad ibn Amr except Quraysh."
"7953","7949 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Truffles are from manna, and their water is healing for the eye, and ajwah (dates) are from Paradise, and they are healing from poison. And this hadith we do not know anyone narrated from Muhammad ibn Amr except Said ibn Amir."
"7954","7950 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. He said: Then a man of Quraysh passed dragging his lower garment, and he said: O son of my brother, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. He said: We have heard what you say. Then he passed by him a second time, and he said to him the like of that. He said: We have heard what you say; if you return, I will carry you upon my shoulder and throw you to the ground. Abu Hurayrah said: And I will not return."
"7955","7951 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Religion remains manifest as long as people hasten the breaking of the fast; the Jews and Christians delay."
"7956","7952 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah. When they say: There is no god but Allah, they have protected from me their blood and wealth except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah."
"7957","7953 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the recitation of a man and said: Who is this? They said: Abd Allah ibn Qays. He said: He has been given from the flutes of the family of Dawud."
"7958","7954 - And Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated it to us, he said: Amr ibn Khalifah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"7959","7955 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that his companions said: We find in ourselves what we do not like to speak of, though for us is what the sun rises upon. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you found this? They said: Yes. He said: That is clear faith."
"7960","7956 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Four rivers gushed from Paradise: Sayhan, Jayhan, the Nile, and the Euphrates."
"7961","7957 - And Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Death is brought on the Day of Resurrection - Yazid said: I think - in the form of a black-and-white ram. It is said: O people of Paradise! So they look out, fearful and afraid lest they exit what they are in. It is said: Do you know this? They say: Our Lord, this is death. Then he says: O people of the Fire! So they look out, joyful and glad to exit what they are in. He says: Do you know this? They say: Yes, this is death. So it is commanded and slaughtered. Then it is said to both groups: Eternity, no death in it ever."
"7962","7958 - And Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not for the Hijrah, I would be a man of the Ansar. And if people take a valley or a path and the Ansar take a valley, I would take the valley of the Ansar and their path."
"7963","7959 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves the Ansar, Allah loves him, and whoever hates the Ansar, Allah hates him."
"7964","7960 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best women who rode camels are the women of Quraysh: the most tender to an orphan in his childhood, and the most caring for a husband in his possessions."
"7965","7961 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: that he used to pray, saying takbir whenever he raised and lowered, and when he finished he said: I am the most like you in prayer to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7966","7962 - And Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"7967","7963 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Saddles are not tied except to three mosques: my mosque, the Sacred Mosque, and al-Aqsa Mosque."
"7968","7964 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, and from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Madinah - whoever commits an offense in it, or shelters an offender, or takes as ally other than his masters, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; neither sarf nor adl is accepted from him."
"7969","7965 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he raised it (to the Prophet), he said: The excellence of congregational prayer over a man's prayer alone is twenty-five degrees."
"7970","7966 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wisal. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you practice wisal! He said: You are not like me; I spend the night with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink. And I know only that he said: So take upon yourselves of deeds what you can bear."
"7971","7967 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The angels continue to pray for one of you as long as he remains in his place of prayer in which he prayed, as long as he does not stand or break his ablution. They say: O Allah, forgive him; O Allah, have mercy on him."
"7972","7968 - And Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, blessed and exalted, said: Who is more unjust than one who creates like My creation? Let them create a mosquito, or let them create an atom."
"7973","7969 - And Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution from what fire has touched, even from a piece of cottage cheese. So Ibn Abbas said: O Abu Hurayrah, do you perform ablution with hot water heated over fire, and with oil cooked over fire? He said: O son of my brother, when you hear a hadith narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), do not strike examples for it."
"7974","7970 - And Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."
"7975","7971 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah, blessed and exalted, descends to the lowest heaven in the last half of the night, or the third. He says: Who is it that calls upon Me that I may answer him? Who is it that asks Me that I may give him? Who is it that seeks My forgiveness that I may forgive him? Until dawn breaks and the early comer leaves the Fajr prayer."
"7976","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bowed in prayer, then raised his head and said: O Allah, save Ayyash ibn Abi Rabiah and Salamah ibn Hisham and al-Walid ibn al-Walid; O Allah, press hard Your grip upon Mudar, and make them years upon them like the years of Yusuf; then he said the takbir and fell down prostrate."
"7977","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in what he narrates from his Lord: Every deed of the son of Adam is his; the good deed is ten times its like up to seven hundredfold, and fasting is Mine and I reward for it; he leaves food and leaves drink and his desire for My sake, so it is Mine and I reward for it."
"7978","And Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the lowest of the people of Paradise in rank is one who makes a wish upon Allah, and it is said: That is yours, and its like with it. Abu Said said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That and ten times its like."
"7979","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever loves meeting Allah, Allah loves meeting him, and whoever hates meeting Allah, Allah hates meeting him."
"7980","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Khalifah al-Bakrawi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Satan confronted me in my prayer, so I seized his neck and strangled him, and I indeed feel the coolness of his tongue upon my palm; and were it not for the supplication of my brother Sulayman, he would have remained tied up with you looking at him. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, except Amr ibn Khalifah, and he is the brother of Hawdhah ibn Khalifah."
"7981","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one endures its hardship and strain - meaning Madinah - except that I will be an intercessor or a witness for him on the Day of Resurrection; and no one leaves it out of dislike for it except that Allah replaces therein one better than him; and Madinah is better for them if they only knew. And he said: Indeed it expels filth just as the bellows expels the dross of iron."
"7982","Muhammad ibn Bashshar and Abu Musa narrated to us, they said: Amr ibn Khalifah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Abdullah ibn Ubayy while he was in the shade of a fortress, and he said: Ibn Abi Kabshah has raised dust over us. So his son Abdullah ibn Abdullah said: O Messenger of Allah, by the One who honored you, if you wish I will bring you his head. He said: No, but be dutiful to your father and keep good company with him. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Muhammad ibn Amr except Amr ibn Khalifah, and he is trustworthy."
"7983","Abu Musa and Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, they said: Amr ibn Khalifah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about coitus interruptus, and he said: Indeed the Jews claim that it is the minor buried-alive girl. Then he said: The Jews have lied. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Muhammad ibn Amr except Amr ibn Khalifah."
"7984","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Khalifah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A woman afflicted with madness came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah for me. So he said: If you wish I will supplicate to Allah for you and He will cure you, and if you wish you will endure patiently and there will be no reckoning upon you. She said: Rather I will endure patiently and there will be no reckoning upon me."
"7985","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Khalifah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a Bedouin: Has Umm Mildam ever seized you? He said: What is Umm Mildam? He said: Heat that occurs between the skin and the flesh. He said: No. He said: Has headache ever seized you? He said: And what is headache? He said: A vein that throbs in a person in his head. He said: I have never experienced this at all. So when he turned away, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased to look at a man from the people of the Fire, let him look at this one."
"7986","And Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Khalifah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a man lying on his stomach, and he said: Indeed this is a lying posture that Allah does not love."
"7987","And Muhammad ibn al-Hisn al-Hadari narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"7988","And Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Khalifah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The orphan girl is to be consulted regarding herself; if she remains silent then that is her permission, and if she refuses then there is no binding upon her."
"7989","And Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated it to us, he said: al-Firyabi narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"7990","And Muhammad ibn Hashim Abu Sahl narrated to us, he said: Abu Hudhayfah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similar to it."
"7991","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is an imam, let him lighten, for behind him are the weak and the elderly and the one with a need; and when he prays by himself, let him lengthen as he wishes."
"7992","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the children of the polytheists, and he said: Allah knows best what they would have done."
"7993","And Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated it to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the heedless ones, and he said: Allah knows best what they would have done. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it with this wording except Abu Usamah."
"7994","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves a debt or a dependent, then it is upon me."
"7995","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba and muzaffat vessels, and said: Every intoxicant is forbidden."
"7996","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr informed us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Whoever washes a dead person, let him take a bath; and whoever carries him, let him perform ablution; and whoever follows a funeral procession, let him not sit until it is placed down."
"7997","And Yahya ibn Hakim narrated it to us, he said: Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"7998","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he saw a man following a pigeon, and he said: A devil following a devil."
"7999","And Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something like it. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who reported it with a connected chain from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, except Hammad ibn Salamah and Muhammad ibn Abdullah; and Sharik differed from them and narrated it from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Aishah; and others besides those we named mention it from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, disconnected."
"8000","And Ali ibn Said al-Masruqi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed you dispute before me, and perhaps some of you are more eloquent in his argument than others, so I judge for him according to what I hear from him; so whoever I judge for him something of his brother's right, let him not take it, for I am only cutting for him a piece of the Fire."
"8001","And Said ibn Bahr al-Qaratisiyy and Abdah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Bishr informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, except Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman and Muhammad ibn Bishr."
"8002","Al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Abbad and Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad - whose name is Abd al-Wahid ibn Wasil - narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Trial does not cease to afflict the believing man and the believing woman until he meets Allah the Exalted with no sin upon him."
"8003","Al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lifespans of my nation are between sixty and seventy, and the fewest of them are those who pass beyond that. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, except Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad."
"8004","Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is granted something as a life-grant, it is his. And this hadith is only known from Abu Salamah from Jabir; thus al-Zuhri narrated it, and Amr ibn Ali narrated it from Muhammad ibn Amr from Abu Salamah from Jabir."
"8005","Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali narrated it to us, from Umar ibn Ali, from Muhammad ibn Amr. And Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Ahmasi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to stand until his feet swelled, and it was said to him: O Messenger of Allah, do you do this when there has come to you from Allah that He has forgiven you what preceded of your sin and what remained?! He said: Shall I not be a grateful slave. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, except al-Muharibi. And al-Amash narrated it from Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah; more than one narrated it from al-Amash."
"8006","Muhammad ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Among the supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: O Allah, grant me enjoyment of my hearing and my sight, and make them the inheritors from me, and grant me victory over whoever wrongs me, and show me my vengeance upon him. And this hadith, we do not retain it from the hadith of Muhammad ibn Amr except from the hadith of al-Muharibi."
"8007","And Muhammad ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The religion will not cease to be manifest as long as people hasten the breaking of the fast; indeed the Jews and the Christians delay it."
"8008","Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, he said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two sons of al-As are believers: Hisham and Amr. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Muhammad, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"8009","Abdullah ibn Abi Thumamah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a funeral and stood for it, and it was said: It is the funeral of a Jew. So he said: Death is a fright. And this hadith, I do not know anyone who narrated it from Muhammad, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"8010","Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Muhammad al-Wariq narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The morsel of Khaybar has not ceased to recur to me until now is the time it has cut my aorta. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Muhammad, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, except Said ibn Muhammad, and he heard it only from Ibrahim ibn Said; and Said ibn Muhammad is not strong, and a group of the people of knowledge narrated from him and tolerated his hadith, and he was from the people of Kufah."
"8011","Ibrahim ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is your chief, O Banu Salimah? They said: al-Jadd ibn Qays, though we consider him miserly. He said: And what disease is more diseased than miserliness? Rather your chief is Bishr ibn al-Bara ibn Marur. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Muhammad ibn Amr except Said ibn Muhammad."
"8012","Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus informed us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Disputation about the Quran is disbelief."
"8013","And Abdah narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bishr informed us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Quran was revealed upon seven letters, and disputation about the Quran is disbelief."
"8014","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us - and the wording is that of Muhammad ibn Mamar - they said: Amr ibn Khalifah al-Bakrawi informed us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he intended a journey, would draw lots among his wives, and the lot fell upon Aishah in the expedition of Banu al-Mustaliq; then when it was the middle of the night, Aishah went out for a need, and her necklace came undone, so she went seeking it; and Mistah was an orphan of Abu Bakr and among his dependents; then when Aishah returned she did not see the army. He said: And Safwan ibn al-Muattal al-Sulami used to lag behind the people, so he would come upon the cup and the bag and the water-skin; I think he said: Is this Aishah? He said: He turned his face away from her, then brought his camel near her. He said: Then he reached the army, and they said a saying, or they spoke about it; then he mentioned the hadith until he finished. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would come and stand at the door and say: How is she? Until one day he came and said: Rejoice, O Aishah, for Allah has revealed your exoneration. So she said: We praise Allah, we do not praise you. He said: And ten verses were revealed concerning that: {Indeed those who brought the slander are a band among you}. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) flogged Mistah and Hamnah and Hassan. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayrah except from this angle with this chain."
"8015","Ibrahim ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us on Friday and mentioned a surah. He said: Then Abu Dharr said to Ubayy: When was this surah revealed? So he turned away from him; then when he finished he said: You have nothing of your prayer except what you engaged in idly. So he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: He spoke the truth. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Hammad ibn Salamah and Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata; so we mentioned it from Hammad ibn Salamah due to the superiority of Hammad over Abd al-Wahhab."
"8016","Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: That a spokesman of Khuzaah said. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Hammad ibn Salamah with this chain."
"8017","Ibrahim ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Aswad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: If there is healing in anything you treat yourselves with, then it is in cupping."
"8018","Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: O Banu Bayadah, marry off Abu Hind; then he mentioned the story of the cupping which Aswad narrated."
"8019","Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Abbad al-Muhallabi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: When there was revealed upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): {And warn your nearest kin}, he said: O Banu Hashim, O Banu Abd al-Muttalib, O Fatimah daughter of Muhammad, O Safiyyah aunt of the Prophet, O Abbas, I do not avail you against Allah in anything; ask me afterwards whatever you wish of my wealth."
"8020","Uqbah ibn Sinan narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Uthman al-Ghatafani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: al-Harith al-Ghatafani came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, share the dates of Madinah with us equally, or else we will fill it against you with horses and men. So he said: Until I consult the two Sads, Sad ibn Ubadah and Sad ibn Muadh - meaning he would consult them - so they said: By Allah, we never gave humiliation of ourselves in the pre-Islamic age, so how now that Allah has brought Islam? So al-Harith returned to him and informed him, and he said: You have betrayed, O Muhammad. He said: So Hassan said: al-Sakhbar. He said: So al-Harith said: Restrain from us, O Muhammad, the tongue of Hassan; for if the water of the sea were mixed with it, it would taint it. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, except Uthman ibn Uthman, and we heard it only from Uqbah ibn Sinan. He narrated to us this hadith and another hadith from Uthman which we heard only from him; as for the other hadith."
"8021","So Uqbah ibn Sinan narrated to us, he said: Uthman narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - no lamentation was performed over him."
"8022","Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: That a man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the time of the dawn prayer; so he prayed the first day and darkened it, then brightened on the next day, and said: Where is the questioner about the time? What is between them is the time. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Abu Usamah and Yahya al-Umawi. And al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated it from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning all the prayer times."
"8023","And Ibrahim ibn Said narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had intended not to accept a gift except from a Qurashi or an Ansari or a Thaqafi. And it has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah from another angle - or a Dawsi. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Muhammad ibn Amr except Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi, and we heard it only from Ibrahim ibn Said."
"8024","Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Uqayli narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The arrogant will be gathered in the forms of ants on the Day of Resurrection. And this hadith, we heard it only from Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Uqayli, from Muhammad ibn Rashid."
"8025","Muhammad ibn Mirdas al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Bakr ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said on the day of sacrifice: Whoever slaughtered - I think he said: before our prayer - let him repeat his sacrifice. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayrah except from this angle, nor did anyone narrate it from Muhammad ibn Amr except Bakr ibn Sulayman; and Bakr is a man well-known for biography; he heard the expeditions and the subject from Ibn Ishaq."
"8026","And Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered a garden, and a camel came and prostrated to him, so they said: We are more entitled to prostrate to you. So he said: If I were to command anyone to prostrate to anyone, I would command the woman to prostrate to her husband. And this hadith was narrated from Muhammad ibn Amr by Abu Usamah and al-Nadr ibn Shumayl."
"8027","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by people shooting and said: Shoot, O sons of Ismail, for your father was an archer. And this hadith has been narrated by more than one from Muhammad from Abu Salamah disconnected."
"8028","Sahl ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Fadalalah ibn Husayn narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When perfume is placed before one of you, let him take some of it and not refuse it; and when sweetmeat is placed before one of you, let him eat of it and not refuse it. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, except Fadalalah ibn Husayn, nor from Fadalalah except Abdullah ibn al-Muthanna."
"8029","Sahl ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform ablution from what fire has altered, even from lumps of dried yogurt. So Abu Salamah said: Does not one of us anoint himself with milk? He said: O my son, when the hadith comes from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), do not strike examples for it. And we do not know Hammad ibn Zayd reported with a connected chain from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, except this hadith."
"8030","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Jazari narrated to us, he said: Murajim ibn al-Awwam ibn Murajim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a noble man of a people comes to you, honor him. And in this hadith there is an addition: That Jarir ibn Abdullah al-Bajali came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he cast his garment for him to sit upon. And he said: When a noble man of a people comes to you, honor him. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayrah except from this angle, nor did anyone narrate it from Muhammad ibn Amr except Murajim."
"8031","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Maymun narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us from Awf, from al-Hasan, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - raised - he said: I do not combine upon My slave two fears and two securities; if I frighten him in this world I grant him security in the Hereafter, and if I grant him security in this world I frighten him in the Hereafter."
"8032","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"8033","Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Sahl ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The anger of Allah intensified upon a people who smashed the egg upon the head of His prophet while he was calling them to Allah. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Hammad ibn Salamah with this chain."
"8034","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Fatimah bint Qays: Go to the house of Umm Sharik, and do not preempt us regarding yourself. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Muhammad, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, except Ibn Idris. And others besides Ibn Idris narrated it from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Fatimah bint Qays; and we heard it only from Yusuf, from Ibn Idris."
"8035","Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Asbat narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed that Safiyyah had menstruated. He said: I see her as nothing but detaining us. They said: She has already performed the farewell circumambulation on the day of sacrifice. He said: Then let her depart. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Muhammad, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, except Asbat."
"8036","Muhammad ibn Ziyad, known as Ibn Zayd al-Mazari, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to love the good omen and hate pessimism."
"8037","Ibrahim ibn Rashid narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Awf narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: When it was the day of the Conquest, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to the mother of Uthman ibn Talhah: Send to me the key of the Kabah. So she said: No, by al-Lat and al-Uzza, I will not send it to you. So someone said: Send to her by force. Then her son Uthman said: O Messenger of Allah, she is fresh from disbelief, so send me to her until I bring it to you. He said: So he went to her and said: O mother, a matter has come other than what was, and if you do not give me the key I will be killed! He said: So she brought it out and handed it to him, and he came with it hastening; then when he drew near the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he stumbled and the key slipped from his hand, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and bent over it with his garment and took it; then he came to the door - I think he said: and opened it - then he stood at the corners and sides of the House supplicating, then prayed two rakahs between the two pillars."
"8038","What Urwah narrated from Abu Hurayrah; Ibn Shihab from Urwah. Abu al-Husayn Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed us, he said: Ahmad ibn Amr al-Bazzar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Said ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah and Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Qabisah ibn Dhuayb and Urwah ibn al-Zubayr and Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade marrying a woman together with her paternal aunt and together with her maternal aunt. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Urwah and Qabisah and Ubaydullah, from Abu Hurayrah, combining them, except Uqayl; nor did anyone narrate it from Uqayl except Yahya ibn Ayyub and Ibn Lahiah."
"8039","Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Urwah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, is Gentle and loves gentleness, and gives upon it what He does not give upon harshness. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Abu Hurayrah, except Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr, and he is lenient in hadith."
"8040","And Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Saigh al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from the nephew of al-Zuhri, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Satan comes to one of you and says: Who created such and such, until he says: So who created Allah? So when one of you sees anything of that, let him say: I believe in Allah. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Abu Hurayrah, except the nephew of al-Zuhri. And Hisham narrated it from his father from Abu Hurayrah, and it was narrated from Abu Hurayrah from various angles."
"8041","Muhammad ibn Jafar from Urwah. Ahmad ibn Muhammad Abu Uthman, nephew of Waki, and Ahmad ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, they said: Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn al-Zubayr, from Urwah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the prayer of fear with the people, so he split the people into two groups; a party stood behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and a party facing the enemy; so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with those behind him - I think he said - one rakah, and prostrated with them two prostrations; then they stood with him, and when he stood upright, those behind him went back behind them, and those others advanced - I think - so he prayed with them one rakah and two prostrations."
"8042","Abu al-Aswad from Urwah. Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qatii narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Madinah expels filth just as the bellows expels the dross of iron; no one leaves it out of dislike for it except that Allah replaces - meaning with one who is better than him. And Abu al-Aswad narrated from Urwah from Abu Hurayrah hadiths, all of them from the hadith of Ibn Lahiah, so we mentioned this hadith from them. Hisham from his father from Abu Hurayrah."
"8043","Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan comes to one of you - I think he said - and says: Who created Allah? So when one of you sees anything of that, let him say: I believe in Allah."
"8044","Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best charity is that which is from surplus wealth, and let one of you begin with those he supports."
"8045","And Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Ubaydah al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Urwah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something like it. And we do not know Abu al-Zinad reported with a connected chain from Urwah from Abu Hurayrah other than this hadith, and it is known from the hadith of Hisham."
"8046","Muhammad ibn Yusuf ibn Sabiq narrated to us, he said: Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man was reckoned, and no good was found for him except a branch of thorns which he removed from the road, so he was forgiven. And this hadith Hisham narrated from his father, and there was disagreement in its chain; and thus Abu Muawiyah narrated it."
"8047","And Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman was punished for a cat which she confined until it died of hunger; she neither fed it nor released it to eat of the vermin of the earth. And this hadith has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah by various paths."
"8048","And Salm ibn Junadah Abu al-Saib narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The last of the villages of Islam to fall into ruin is Madinah. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayrah except from this angle with this chain, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Hisham except Junadah, and we heard it only from Salm from his father."
"8049","Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Hassan ibn Ghalib narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Malik, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Salamah ibn al-Azraq, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a funeral being wept over, and I was with him and Umar ibn al-Khattab, and Umar rebuked them. So he said: Leave them, O son of al-Khattab, for the soul is afflicted, and the eye is tearful, and the covenant is recent."
"8050","And Umar narrated to us, he said: Hassan ibn Ghalib narrated to us, he said: al-Layth - meaning Ibn Sad - narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something like it. And this hadith was narrated by more than one from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Salamah ibn al-Azraq, from Abu Hurayrah; and I think al-Layth erred in its chain, and we do not know anyone who followed al-Layth upon his narration."
"8051","Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah from Abu Hurayrah. Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Abu Hurayrah and Zayd ibn Khalid and Shibl ibn Mabad, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the slave-girl who commits adultery before she is married, and he said: If she commits adultery then flog her, then if she commits adultery then flog her, then he said on the third or fourth: Then sell her even for a rope. And this hadith has been narrated by more than one from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Abu Hurayrah; and we do not know anyone who said: from Abu Hurayrah and Zayd ibn Khalid and Shibl ibn Mabad, except Ibn Uyaynah."
"8052","And Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Ibn Uyaynah informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Abu Hurayrah and Zayd - meaning Ibn Khalid - and Shibl ibn Mabad, that two men disputed before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); then one of them said: O Messenger of Allah, judge between us by the Book of Allah. Then the other said - and he was the more learned of them - Yes, O Messenger of Allah, judge between us by the Book of Allah and permit me to speak. He said: Speak. He said: My son was a hired worker for this one, and he committed adultery with a woman; then I was told that upon my son is stoning, so I ransomed him with a hundred sheep and a slave-girl; then I asked men of the people of knowledge, and they told me that upon my son is a hundred lashes and exile for a year. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose Hand is my soul, I will judge between you two by the Book of Allah; as for the sheep and the slave-girl, they are returned to you, and upon your son is a hundred lashes and exile for a year; and go, O Unays, to the wife of this one, and if she confesses then stone her. So she confessed, and he stoned her."
"8053","Zuhayr ibn Muhammad al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the one who drinks standing knew what is upon him, he would vomit. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Abu Hurayrah, except Mamar, nor from Mamar except Abd al-Razzaq."
"8054","Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating from al-Numan - meaning Ibn Rashid - from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Abu Hurayrah: That a Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Allah, have mercy upon me and Muhammad, and have mercy upon no one with us. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have constricted something vast. Then the Bedouin stood and urinated in the mosque, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pour over his urine a bucket of water. Al-Zuhri narrated it from Said from Abu Hurayrah, and Ibn Uyaynah narrated it from him, and Ibn Abi Hafsah narrated it from al-Zuhri from Said and Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah; and we do not know anyone who said: from Ubaydullah from Abu Hurayrah, except al-Numan and Shuayb."
"8055","And Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating from al-Numan, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no pessimism, and I love the good omen. It was said: And what is the good omen? He said: The good word which one of you hears. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Abu Hurayrah, except al-Numan; and al-Numan is sound in hadith."
"8056","And Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A Bedouin stood and urinated in the mosque, and the people seized him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pour over his urine a bucket of water, or a bucketful of water, for you were only sent as facilitators and were not sent as complicators."
"8057","Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah and Ubaydullah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of the dwellings of the Ansar are Banu al-Najjar. They said: Then who, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Then Banu al-Harith ibn al-Khazraj. They said: Then who, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Then Banu Saidah. They said: Then who, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Then in every dwelling of the Ansar there is good."
"8058","Ismail ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Abbad Abu Safwan narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I had the like of Uhud in gold, it would please me that three nights not pass over me while I have anything of it with me, except something I set aside for a debt."
"8059","Ahmad ibn al-Faraj al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Suwayd al-Ramli narrated to us, he said: Yunus narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman and Ibn al-Musayyib and Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah and Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman said, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the noon or afternoon prayer and greeted at two rakahs; then Dhu al-Shimalayn Ibn Amr ibn Nadlah al-Khuzai - and he was an ally of Banu Zuhrah - said to him: Has it been shortened or did you forget, O Messenger of Allah? He said: I did not forget and it was not shortened. Dhu al-Shimalayn said: Some of that has occurred. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to the people and said: Has Dhu al-Shimalayn spoken the truth? They said: Yes. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and completed the prayer, and prostrated two prostrations while sitting."
"8060","Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub and Ibn Lahiah, from Uqayl - meaning Ibn Khalid - from al-Zuhri, from Qabisah ibn Dhuayb and Urwah ibn al-Zubayr and Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade marrying a woman together with her paternal aunt and together with her maternal aunt."
"8061","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, as far as I know, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There was a man who gave loans to people, and he said to his youths - or to his youth: When the insolvent one is in hardship, overlook him, that perhaps Allah will overlook us. Then when he met Allah, He overlooked him. Al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah."
"8062","Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, concerning the statement of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: {Indeed I see in the dream that I sacrifice you}. He said: al-Qasim - meaning Ibn Muhammad - informed me, he said: Abu Hurayrah and Kab gathered, and Abu Hurayrah began narrating from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Kab began narrating from the Books. Then Abu Hurayrah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For every prophet there is an answered supplication, and I have stored my supplication as intercession for my nation. So Kab said: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. He said: May my father and mother be ransom for him. And I will tell you about Ibrahim; then he mentioned the story of Ibrahim regarding the sacrifice. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Qasim except al-Zuhri."
"8063","Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Badal ibn al-Muhabbar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Mansur, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, accepts charity, and does not accept of it except the pure; He accepts it with His Right Hand, Blessed and Exalted, and nurtures it for His slave just as one of you nurtures his foal or his young camel."
"8064","And al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from Ayyub, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. And this hadith has been narrated by some of the companions of Abd al-Razzaq, from Mamar, from Ayyub, from a man, from al-Qasim, from Abu Hurayrah; so they hold that Ayyub heard it from Abbad ibn Mansur. And Abd al-Wahid ibn Sibrah reported it with a connected chain from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah."
"8065","Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated it to us, he said: Said ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Sibrah, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, accepts charity, and does not accept of it - I think he said - except the pure; He accepts it with His Right Hand, Blessed and Exalted, and nurtures it for His slave just as one of you nurtures his colt or his young camel, until he meets Him on the Day of Resurrection like Uhud."
"8066","Sulayman ibn Yasar from Abu Hurayrah. Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah and Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8067","And Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah and Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed the Jews and the Christians do not dye, so oppose them. And this hadith has been narrated by more than one from al-Zuhri with this chain, so we sufficed with the narration of those I mentioned."
"8068","Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ibrahim ibn Abi Amr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, has a pillar of light before the Throne; then when the slave says: There is no god but Allah, that pillar shakes. So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: Be still. So it says: How can I be still when You have not forgiven its speaker? So He says: I have forgiven him, and it becomes still at that. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this angle with this chain; and Abdullah ibn Ibrahim ibn Abi Amrah is not strong in hadith, and we only mentioned this hadith for the beauty of its wording."
"8069","Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Attaf ibn Khalid informed us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Aban ibn Uthman, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever frees a believing neck, Allah frees, for every limb of him, a limb of it from the Fire. And this hadith has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah from other angles, and we do not know it narrated from Sulayman ibn Yasar from Abu Hurayrah except from this angle; and Attaf is not strong, and a group of the people of knowledge narrated from him and tolerated his hadith."
"8070","Sahl ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ibn Lahiah, he said: Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj informed me, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition, and Abu Hurayrah was among them, and he said: If you meet Habbar ibn al-Aswad and Nafi ibn Abd Amr, burn them with fire, and do not kill them. And they had jabbed Zaynab daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when she left Makkah for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she remained ill until she died. Then when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bade us farewell he said: I had commanded you to burn Habbar and Nafi, but it is not fitting for anyone to punish with the punishment of Allah; so if you meet them, kill them."
"8071","And Ibn Salih ibn Muadh narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Layth, from Bukayr, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, with something similar or close to it, as far as I know that Salih narrated to me."
"8072","Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, he said: Said ibn al-Hakam ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahiah informed me, he said: Abu al-Aswad narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am a guarantor, upon Allah, for a man who goes out in the path of Allah seeking the pleasure of Allah and striving in His path, that He admit him to Paradise or return him to his family with what he obtained of reward and spoils."
"8073","Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf from Abu Hurayrah. Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Ali ibn Suwayd ibn Manjuf narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Were it not that I would burden my nation, I would command them to use the tooth-stick with every prayer."
"8074","Ahmad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Rawh narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd - meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman - from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever fasts Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, he is forgiven what preceded of his sin. And this hadith Ibn Uyaynah narrates from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah; and we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Zuhri from Humayd except Malik."
"8075","Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd, from Abu Hurayrah."
"8076","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and the wording is the wording of Mamar - that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, he had intercourse with his wife in Ramadan by day. So he said: Free a neck. He said: I do not have. He said: Fast two consecutive months. He said: I cannot. He said: Then feed sixty poor persons. He said: I cannot find. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a basket containing dates, and he said: Where is the man who said what he said just now? Take this and give it in charity. He said: By the One who sent you with the truth, there is no household between its two lava-fields more in need of it than us. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed until we saw his molars, then said: Take it and eat it, and spend it upon your dependents."
"8077","And Yahya ibn Khalaf narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Ala ibn Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, he said: al-Zuhri narrated to me, from Humayd, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Ramadan and said: O Messenger of Allah, he had intercourse with his wife by day. So he said: Woe to you, free a neck. He said: I do not have. He said: Fast two consecutive months. He said: O Messenger of Allah, did I meet what I met except in fasting. He said: Then feed sixty poor persons. He said: I cannot find. He said: Sit. Then a man came with his charity carrying it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Where is the man who spoke just now? Take this and give it in charity upon yourself. He said: O Messenger of Allah, is charity except upon a dependent; by the One who sent you with the truth, there is none between its two lava-fields more needy than us. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed until his molars appeared, and said: Take it and eat it and spend it upon your dependents."
"8078","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Malik, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd, from Abu Hurayrah: That a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I broke fast one day in the month of Ramadan. He said: Free a neck; then he mentioned something similar. And this hadith, they hold that Malik erred in it; rather the narration that is established from al-Zuhri, from Humayd, from Abu Hurayrah, is: That a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I fell upon my wife - and it is the correct one. Ibn Uyaynah and Mamar and Ismail ibn Umayyah and Muhammad ibn Ishaq and Mansur ibn al-Mutamir narrated it."
"8079","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, from Muammal ibn Ismail, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Mansur, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And Hisham ibn Sad narrated it and erred in its chain, so he narrated it from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah; and the meaning in it is one even if the wordings differed."
"8080","Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Shuayb - meaning Ibn Hamzah - informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A man was excessive upon himself until when death came to him he said to his family: When I die, burn me, then crush me, then scatter me in the wind; for by Allah, if Allah decrees upon me He will punish me with a punishment He punishes none of His creation with. He said: So his family did that with him. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said to everything that took anything of him: Render what you took; and there he was standing. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: What carried you to do what you did? He said: Fear of You. So Allah forgave him."
"8081","And Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Abu Hafs al-Tinnisi narrated to us, he said: Sadaqah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar. Sadaqah said: And Ibn Saman narrated to me, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"8082","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, he said: Mamar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever spends two pairs of his wealth, the angels call him; so whoever was of the people of striving is called from the gate of striving, and whoever was of the people of fasting is called from the gate of al-Rayyan. Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, there is no harm upon a man from whichever gate he is called, but is anyone called from them all? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed I hope you are among them. This hadith has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah from other angles, and we do not know for it a path from Abu Hurayrah better than this path."
"8083","Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The strong is not the wrestler. They said: Then who is the strong? He said: The one who controls himself at anger. And this hadith has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah from other angles, and this chain is the soundest chain narrated from Abu Hurayrah concerning that."
"8084","Ismail ibn Masud al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Umar ibn Said, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears - or whoever says in his oath: By al-Lat - let him say: There is no god but Allah."
"8085","And Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Mamar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever says to his companion: I will gamble with you, let him give charity; and whoever says in his oath: By al-Lat, let him say: There is no god but Allah."
"8086","Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every newborn is born upon the natural disposition, so his parents make him a Jew and make him a Christian. And this hadith Mamar narrated from al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and we do not know anyone who said: from al-Zuhri from Humayd from Abu Hurayrah, except Muhammad ibn Yusuf from al-Awzai from al-Zuhri."
"8087","And Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abi Shuayb narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the slave-girl of one of you commits adultery, let him flog her; then if she commits adultery, let him sell her even for a rope. And this hadith the trustworthy narrate from al-Zuhri from Ubaydullah from Abu Hurayrah and Zayd ibn Khalid."
"8088","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8089","And Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated it to us, he said: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Adam and Musa argued; so Musa said: You are Adam who expelled your offspring from Paradise. So Adam said to him: You are Musa whom Allah chose with His messages and His speech, yet you blame me for a matter decreed upon me before I was created. He said: So Adam overcame Musa. And this hadith has been narrated from al-Zuhri by various paths, and there was disagreement upon al-Zuhri in the narration of this hadith. So Mamar narrated it from al-Zuhri from Abu Salamah, and Said ibn al-Musayyib narrated it from Abu Hurayrah, and Ibrahim ibn Sad and Shuayb narrated it from al-Zuhri from Humayd. And Umar ibn Said narrated it from al-Zuhri from al-Araj."
"8090","And Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Yaman al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Shuayb narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Time draws near, and knowledge is taken away, and trials appear, and miserliness is cast, and al-harj increases. They said: And what is al-harj? He said: Killing, killing. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Zuhri from Humayd except Shuayb; and Mamar narrated it from al-Zuhri from Said from Abu Hurayrah."
"8091","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from al-Numan ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Said, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is in prayer, let him not spit before him nor to his right, but to his left or under his left foot. And this hadith is narrated by more than one from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Said; and al-Numan combined from al-Zuhri, from Humayd, from Abu Humayd, from Abu Said and Abu Hurayrah."
"8092","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us - as far as I know - they said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from al-Numan ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that when he sought rain he turned his cloak and faced the qiblah. And this hadith al-Numan erred in, and none from al-Zuhri followed him upon this narration, because the trustworthy narrate it from al-Zuhri from Abbad ibn Tamim from his uncle."
"8093","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: It is not fitting for a slave to say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta."
"8094","And Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had intended to command the prayer to be established, then go to the dwellings of people who do not attend the prayer and burn them upon them."
"8095","Ibrahim ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: al-Masudi narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Humayd, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Quraysh and the Ansar and Aslam and Ghifar and Muzaynah and Ashja are allies; they have no ally besides Allah and His Messenger. And this hadith, there has been disagreement upon Sad in its narration; so he narrated it from Abu Salamah from Abu Hurayrah, and he narrated it from Humayd, and he narrated it from his father; and we do not know anyone who said: from Humayd, except al-Masudi."
"8096","Ahmad ibn al-Faraj al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Abdullah - meaning Ibn Abi Farwah - narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Were it not that I would burden my nation, I would make the time of the evening prayer up to half the night. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Safwan except Ishaq, and Ishaq is lenient in hadith; and we do not know Safwan narrated from Humayd from Abu Hurayrah except this hadith and another hadith. And it has been narrated from Abu Hurayrah from other angles that he said: Were it not that I would burden my nation, I would delay the evening prayer to a third of the night."
"8097","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The adulterer does not commit adultery while he is a believer when he commits adultery, nor does he steal while he is a believer when he steals, nor does he drink wine while he is a believer when he drinks it, nor does he plunder a plunder - I think he said - of notable worth when he plunders it while he is a believer. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Safwan except Abd al-Aziz. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman except Safwan ibn Sulaym."
"8098","What Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated from Abu Hurayrah. Zayd ibn Akhzam Abu Talib al-Tai narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab informed me from the hadith of Ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he stood, said the takbir; and when he bowed he said the takbir, then said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, raising his spine; then he says while standing: Our Lord, to You is praise; then he said the takbir, then where he prostrates he says the takbir, then he says the takbir when he raises his head, then when he prostrates, then he says the takbir when he raises his head, until he completes his prayer; and he says the takbir when he stands from the two. Abu Hurayrah said: And I am the most like you in prayer to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8099","Muhammad ibn Dawud al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: When a man goes bankrupt - or one who bought merchandise then goes bankrupt - its owner is most entitled to it. And this hadith has been narrated from Yahya ibn Said by a group, among them al-Thawri and others."
"8100","Salim from Abu Hurayrah. Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Humayd narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Mubashshir al-Saidi, from al-Zuhri, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All my nation is pardoned except the open sinners; and indeed among openness is that a man does a deed secretly then informs of it."
"8101","Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah from Abu Hurayrah. Ibrahim ibn Abdullah al-Razi narrated to us - or another of our companions - he said: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, Hammam informed us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah narrated to me, that Abu Hurayrah narrated to him that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed three men among the Children of Israel: a leper and a bald man and a blind man. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, intended to test them, so He sent an angel to them; then he came to the leper and said: What thing is most beloved to you? He said: A good color and a good skin, for people have deemed me filthy. He said: So he wiped him and it went away, and he was given a good color and a good skin. He said: Which wealth is most beloved to you? He said: Camels - or he said: cattle. He said: So he was given a pregnant she-camel. Then he said: May it be blessed for you in it. He said: As for the bald man. He said: What thing is most beloved to you? He said: Good hair, and that this go away from me; people have deemed me filthy. He said: So he wiped him and it went away, and he was given good hair. He said: So which wealth is most beloved to you? He said: Cattle, so he gave him a pregnant cow. And he said: May it be blessed for you in it. And as for the blind man, he said: What thing is most beloved to you? He said: That Allah return my sight to me, so I see people with it. He said: So he wiped him and Allah returned his sight to him. He said: So which wealth is most beloved to you? He said: Sheep, so he gave him a sheep that gives birth; then these two produced offspring, and this one gave birth; so this one had a valley of camels, and this one had a valley of cattle, and this one had a valley of sheep. Then he came to the leper in his form and appearance and said: A poor man whose means have been cut off in his travel; there is no conveyance today except by Allah then by you; I ask you by the One who gave you the good color and the good skin and the wealth, for a camel to convey me upon it in my travel. So he said to him: Rights are many. So he said to him: As if I know you; were you not a poor leper and Allah gave you. So he said: I inherited this wealth from elder to elder. So he said: If you are lying, may Allah return you to what you were. And he came to the bald man in his form and appearance. So he said to him like what he said to this one, and he replied to him like what this one replied to him. So he said: If you are lying, may Allah return you to what you were. And he came to the blind man in his form and said: A poor man and a traveler whose means have been cut off in his travel; there is no conveyance for me today except by Allah then by you; I ask you by the One who returned your sight to you, for a sheep to convey myself with it in my travel. So he said: I was blind and Allah returned my sight to me, and poor, so take what you wish; for by Allah, today I will not praise you nor praise myself for anything you take for Allah. So he said: Hold your wealth, for you were only tested; Allah is pleased with you and angry with your two companions. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this angle with this chain."
"8102","Abd al-Ala ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Hammad - meaning Ibn Salamah - narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, narrating from his Lord, Blessed and Exalted: My slave committed a sin and said: O Lord, forgive me my sin. So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: My slave committed a sin and knew that he has a Lord who forgives sin and seizes for sin. Then he returned and sinned, and said: O Lord, forgive me my sin. So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: My slave committed a sin and knew that he has a Lord who forgives sin and seizes for sin. Then he returned and sinned, and said: O Lord, forgive me my sin. So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: My slave committed a sin and knew that he has a Lord who forgives sin and seizes for sin; do what you wish, for I have forgiven you. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this angle with this chain."
"8103","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar ibn Faris narrated to us, he said: Fulayh - meaning Ibn Sulayman - narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Indeed the first group to enter Paradise is upon the form of the moon on the night of full moon, then those who follow them like the most beautiful brilliant star in the sky; their hearts are upon one heart; for every man among them are two wives of the wide-eyed maidens, the marrow of their shanks seen from behind the flesh."
"8104","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have not given you anything, nor have I withheld it from you; I am only a distributor; I place where I am commanded. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from this angle."
"8105","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave me as I have left you; for those before you perished only by their questioning and their differing upon their prophets; but what I forbid you, refrain from it, and what I command you, do of it what you can."
"8106","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The space of the bow of one of you in Paradise is better than what the sun rises upon and sets."
"8107","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not spy, and do not compete, and do not turn away from one another, and do not hate one another; and be slaves of Allah, brothers."
"8108","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of suspicion, for suspicion is the most lying of speech."
"8109","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah; so when they say: There is no god but Allah, they protect from me their blood and their wealth except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah."
"8110","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you will be saved by his deed. They said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even me, except that Allah envelop me from Him with bounty and mercy; but draw near and give glad tidings."
"8111","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah, from Abu Hurayrah: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am the closest of people to Isa son of Maryam; the prophets are brothers of different mothers; their fathers are diverse."
"8112","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Ali, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise is a tree in whose shade a rider travels a hundred years; recite if you wish: {And extended shade}."
"8113","Al-Walid ibn Rabah from Abu Hurayrah. Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is near that Isa son of Maryam descend as a just judge and an equitable imam; so he will kill the pig and break the cross, and the call will be one."
"8114","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is the mirror of the believer; he guards him from behind him, and protects his loss. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Hurayrah except al-Walid ibn Rabah, nor do we know anyone who narrated it from Kathir except Abu Ahmad."
"8115","Muhammad ibn Miskin ibn Numaylah narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not fitting for the two-faced one to be trustworthy with Allah."
"8116","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The lowest of the Muslims grants protection upon them. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Walid ibn Rabah except Kathir ibn Zayd, nor do we know it narrated from Abu Hurayrah except from this angle."
"8117","And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim also narrated it to us, he said: Mansur ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"8118","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: I will give the banner tomorrow to a man who loves Allah and His Messenger, and Allah and His Messenger love him; then Ali entered, and he had sore eyes, so he spat in his eye, then gave him - meaning the banner - and Allah granted victory upon him."
"8119","And Hamzah ibn Malik ibn Hamzah ibn Farwah ibn Sufyan wrote to me informing me that his uncle Sufyan ibn Hamzah narrated to him, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"8120","And Hamzah ibn Malik wrote to me informing that his uncle Sufyan ibn Hamzah narrated to him from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Muttalib, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: Fasting is Mine and I reward for it; and by the oath of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the breath of the fasting person's mouth is more pleasant with Allah than the scent of musk; so whichever man among you wakes fasting, let him not speak obscenely nor act ignorantly; and if a person fights him, let him say: I am fasting; for they have on the Day of Resurrection a basin which none but the fasting will approach. And this hadith with these wordings and the completion of this speech, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Hurayrah except al-Walid ibn Rabah."
"8121","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayra: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended the minbar and said: Amin, Amin, Amin. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, you would not do this? He said: Indeed Jibril said: May the nose of one upon whom Ramadan enters and then he is not forgiven be rubbed in dust; may the nose of a servant, or: may he be distanced. Then he said: May the nose of a man, or: may he be distanced, who reaches his parents or one of them and then does not enter Paradise, so I said: Amin. Then he said: May the nose of a servant, or a man, or: may he be distanced, in whose presence I am mentioned and he does not send blessings upon you, so I said: Amin."
"8122","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Salama narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayra: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Reconciliation is permissible among the Muslims."
"8123","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not accept prayer without purification, nor charity from misappropriated spoils. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayra except with this chain. And others besides Sulayman narrated it from Kathir."
"8124","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that its trees be cut down or beaten off leaves, meaning: Madinah."
"8125","Muhammad ibn Miskin ibn Numayla narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Wretched is the slave of the dinar and the dirham."
"8126","Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8127","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated it to us, he said: Mansur ibn Salama Abu Salama al-Khuza'i narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When sight enters, there is no permission. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayra except from this angle."
"8128","Zurayq ibn al-Suht narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the people of polytheism let their mustaches grow and trim their beards, so oppose them; let the beards grow and trim the mustaches."
"8129","Zurayq ibn al-Suht narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The ally of a people is from them, and the freed slave of a people is from them, and the son of the sister of a people is from them."
"8130","Zurayq ibn al-Suht narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever deceives us is not from us."
"8131","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Faith is Yemeni and wisdom is Yemeni, and tranquility is among the people of sheep and cattle, and disbelief is toward the east, the loud-voiced people of horses and wool."
"8132","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The lower garment is to the middle of his shin, to the ankles; whatever is below that is in the Fire."
"8133","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: O people, leave me as I have left you; those before you were destroyed only by their many questions and their differing with their prophets. Whatever I command you, do of it what you can, and whatever I forbid you, refrain from it."
"8134","Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Mundhir Isma'il ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate in the house of al-Abbas, or in the house of Hamza, and said: People of my ummah will surely deal freely with what Allah bestowed upon His Messenger, having no share other than it. And expiations for sins are: completing ablution despite hardship, many steps to the mosques, and waiting for prayer after prayer."
"8135","Hamza ibn Malik wrote to me informing me that his uncle Sufyan ibn Hamza narrated to him, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Fatima daughter of the Messenger of Allah, purchase yourself from Allah; I do not avail you against Allah anything. O Safiyya daughter of Abd al-Muttalib, purchase yourself from Allah, for I do not avail you against Allah anything."
"8136","Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated it to us, he said: Ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, from his father, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Walid ibn Zayd, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something like it. And he added in it: O A'isha, purchase yourself from Allah; I do not avail you against Allah anything, even with half a date. O A'isha, let no beggar return from you, even with a burnt hoof."
"8137","Al-Abbas ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Athma narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Walid ibn Rabah, from his father, that he heard Abu Hurayra say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I would not love to have Uhud as gold in my house with a night passing me while in my house is any dinar of it, except that I set it aside for a debt or spending in the path of Allah."
"8138","Hamza ibn Malik wrote to me informing that his uncle Sufyan ibn Hamza narrated to him, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I was favored with six qualities not given to anyone before me: I was forgiven what preceded of my sin and what will follow, spoils were made lawful for me and were not lawful for anyone before me, my ummah was made the best of nations, the earth was made for me a mosque and a purification, I was given al-Kawthar, and I was aided with awe. By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, indeed your companion is the bearer of the banner of praise on the Day of Resurrection; under it will be Adam and those below him."
"8139","Hamza ibn Malik wrote to me informing from his uncle Sufyan ibn Hamza, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from al-Walid ibn Rabah, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: People are the outer garment and the Ansar are the inner garment. Were it not for the Hijrah I would have been a man of the Ansar. If people took a valley and the Ansar took a valley, I would take the mountain path of the Ansar. And you will meet after me favoritism, so be patient until you meet me at the Hawd."
"8140","Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Hurayra; Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Irak: Ahmad ibn Abda narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyayna informed us, from Ayyub ibn Musa and Yazid ibn Yazid, from Makhul, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no charity upon the Muslim for his slave and his horse."
"8141","Al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Shu'ayb al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever catches a rak'a of prayer has caught it. And this hadith has been narrated from Abu Hurayra from more than one angle."
"8142","Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Haywa narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'a, from Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not turn away from your fathers."
"8143","Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Rabi'a, from Irak, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will surely cease raising their eyes to the sky during supplication, lest it be snatched, meaning: or their eyesight be snatched."
"8144","Isma'il ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Khuthaym ibn Irak ibn Malik narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Aslam, may Allah grant it safety, and Ghifar, may Allah forgive it. And this hadith has been narrated from Abu Hurayra from more than one angle, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Irak except Khuthaym, from his father."
"8145","Isma'il ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Khuthaym ibn Irak ibn Malik narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayra: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) employed Siba' ibn Urfuta over Madinah, and he recited: {Woe to the defrauders}. So I said: So-and-so is ruined; he has two measures, a measure he gives with and a measure he takes with. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Abu Hurayra except Irak."
"8146","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik, or another, narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Zayd, from Khuthaym ibn Irak, from his father, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no charity upon the Muslim for his slave and his horse."
"8147","Ahmad ibn Abda narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Uthman ibn Abi Sulayman, from Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Hurayra, he said: I arrived in Madinah while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at Khaybar, and I found a man of Banu Ghifar leading the people in prayer, and he recited in the first rak'a Surah Maryam and in the second {Woe to the defrauders}; I think he said: the Fajr prayer."
"8148","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Abu Salama al-Khuza'i Mansur ibn Salama narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Khuthaym ibn Irak, from his father, from Abu Hurayra: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man becomes bankrupt and one finds - I think he said: a man finds his goods with his companion, he has more right to them. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Irak, from Abu Hurayra, except with this chain, and it has been narrated from Abu Hurayra from more than one angle."
"8149","Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Khuthaym ibn Irak ibn Malik narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he detained upon suspicion. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayra except from this angle."
"8150","Al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Hariri narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Khuthaym ibn Irak ibn Malik narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayra: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took bail in accusation cases. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Abu Hurayra from this angle. And Ibrahim ibn Khuthaym is not strong, and a group narrated from him and accepted his hadith."
"8151","Al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Go gently for Allah's sake, go gently. For Allah, Blessed and Exalted, is severe in punishment; were it not for suckling infants, bowing men, and grazing cattle, punishment would be poured upon you in torrents, or punishment would be sent down upon you. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Abu Hurayra with this chain."
"8152","Al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Khuthaym narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is put in charge of any affair of the Muslims, Allah assigns to him an angel on his right - I think he said - and an angel on his left, guiding and directing him when good is intended for him. And whoever is put in charge of any affair of the Muslims and other than that is intended for him, he is left to himself. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording from Abu Hurayra except from the hadith of Irak ibn Malik."
"8153","Al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Khuthaym ibn Irak narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Three have a right upon Allah that He not reject their supplication: the fasting person until he breaks his fast, the oppressed until he is vindicated, and the traveler until he returns. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it with this wording except Abu Hurayra with this chain."
"8154","Al-Jarrah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Khuthaym ibn Irak ibn Malik narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Caution does not avail against decree, and supplication avails against what the decree has not yet descended upon. And affliction and supplication surely meet between heaven and earth and wrestle until the Day of Resurrection. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated except from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with this chain."
"8155","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from Makhul, from Irak ibn Malik, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): and I found with me in one place: Indeed Allah has ninety-nine names - and in one place - Indeed in Friday there is an hour; so I held back on it until I look into the original."
"8156","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Usama ibn Zayd, from Irak, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no charity upon the Muslim for his horse - I think he said - nor his slave."
"8157","Nu'aym ibn Abdullah al-Mujmir from Abu Hurayra: Fitr ibn Hammad ibn Waqid narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Nu'aym ibn Abdullah al-Mujmir, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed upon the passes of Madinah are angels; neither plague nor the Dajjal shall enter it."
"8158","Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, as far as I know, he said: Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Nu'aym al-Mujmir, from Abu Hurayra: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you prays, then sits in his place, the angels continue to pray for him: O Allah forgive him, O Allah bless him."
"8159","Ahmad ibn Abda narrated to us, he said: Sulaym ibn Akhdar informed me, he said: Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, from Nu'aym ibn Abdullah, from Abu Hurayra: that they asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): How do we send blessings upon you? He said: Say: O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad, and bless Muhammad, and upon the family of Muhammad, as You sent blessings and blessed Ibrahim and the family of Ibrahim in the worlds; indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. And the salam is as you have learned. And this wording we do not recall except from the hadith of Dawud, from Nu'aym, from Abu Hurayra."
"8160","Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sa'd, from Nu'aym ibn Abdullah, he said: I heard Abu Hurayra say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand one day and we set out to the market of Banu Qaynuqa'. When he returned he entered the mosque and sat in it, then al-Hasan came running until he sat in his lap. The Messenger of Allah opened his mouth and put his mouth into his mouth, then said: O Allah, I love him, so love him and love whoever loves him. Abu Hurayra said: I never saw him thereafter except that my eyes overflowed with tears."
"8161","Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, I found it written with me from him, he said: Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: al-Layth narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Yazid, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Nu'aym al-Mujmir, from Abu Hurayra: that he prayed behind him and said: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, then recited the Mother of the Book until he reached {Not of those who earned anger nor of those astray}, he said: Amin, and the people said: Amin. And he says every time he prostrates: Allah is Greatest, and says: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, I am indeed the most like you in prayer to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8162","Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Asbagh narrated to us, from Ibn Wahb, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Nu'aym al-Mujmir, that he said: I prayed behind Abu Hurayra, and he recited {When the sky splits open} and prostrated in it, and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrate in it. Abu al-Ghayth, whose name is Salim, freed slave of Muti', from Abu Hurayra."
"8163","Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from Abu al-Ghayth, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever takes people's wealth intending to repay it, Allah will repay on his behalf; and whoever takes it intending to destroy it, Allah will destroy him. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this angle with this chain."
"8164","Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, as far as I know, and Ibrahim ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Maslama, from Malik, from Thawr ibn Zayd, from Abu al-Ghayth, from Abu Hurayra, he said: Al-Jumu'a was revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he recited it until he reached: {And others of them who have not yet joined them}. They said: Who are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: So he was silent until they said that three times. Then he struck his hand upon Salman, then said: If the religion were at the Pleiades, or attached to the Pleiades, this one and his companions would surely reach it."
"8165","And with his chain: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one who strives for the widow and the poor is like the mujahid in the path of Allah."
"8166","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Thawr, from Abu al-Ghayth, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until a man from Qahtan emerges driving the people with his staff."
"8167","Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Thawr, from Abu al-Ghayth, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Dhu al-Suwayqatayn from Abyssinia will destroy the House of Allah."
"8168","Abu Sufyan, freed slave of Abu Ahmad, from Abu Hurayra: Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Husayn, from Abu Sufyan, freed slave of Abu Ahmad, from Abu Hurayra: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the sale of araya for less than five awsuq."
"8169","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Wazir narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Husayn, from Abu Sufyan, from Abu Hurayra: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed the two prostrations of forgetfulness after the salam."
"8170","Salih, freed slave of al-Taw'ama, from Abu Hurayra: Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah and Qabisa narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salih, freed slave of al-Taw'ama, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let no townsman sell for a bedouin."
"8171","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama narrated to us, he said: Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Salih ibn Nabhan, who is the freed slave of al-Taw'ama, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not turn backs on one another, do not outbid to deceive, do not hate one another, and be servants of Allah, brothers."
"8172","Ibn Karama narrated to us, he said: Qabisa narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Salih, freed slave of al-Taw'ama, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to his wives: It is only this one, then stay to the mats. And this hadith, I think it is from Sufyan, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Salih, but thus Qabisa said. And more than one narrated it from Salih; among them Ibn Abi Dhi'b and Salih ibn Kaysan."
"8173","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Salih, freed slave of al-Taw'ama, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said to his wives: This is the Hajj, then remaining to the mats."
"8174","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Salih, freed slave of al-Taw'ama, from Abu Hurayra: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah. When they say it, they protect from me their blood and wealth except by its right, and their account is upon Allah."
"8175","Al-Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Salih, freed slave of al-Taw'ama, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Say to one who announces a lost item in the mosque: May you not find it."
"8176","Al-Abbas narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Salih, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever washes a dead person, let him perform ghusl."
"8177","Salama ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Salih, freed slave of al-Taw'ama, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere among the mosques, except the Sacred Mosque."
"8178","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ammar, imam of the mosque of Quba who resided at Quba, narrated to us, he said: Salih, freed slave of al-Taw'ama, narrated to us, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The tall, huge one will be brought on the Day of Resurrection and weighed, and will not weigh with Allah the wing of a gnat."
"8179","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ammar narrated to us, from Salih, freed slave of al-Taw'ama, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The molar tooth of the disbeliever is like Uhud, and his seat in the Fire is a journey of three."
"8180","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Bakka'i narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Salih, freed slave of al-Taw'ama, from Abu Hurayra: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, wiped over his leather socks, and prayed."
"8181","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Ja'far ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from the freed slave of al-Taw'ama, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If the world were worth with Allah the wing of a gnat, He would not give a disbeliever anything of it."
"8182","Ibn Silan, from Abu Hurayra: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Jurashi narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Muslim, the henna seller, narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Ibn Silan, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not leave the two rak'as of Fajr, even if horses trample you. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except from this angle with this chain."
"8183","Ahmad ibn al-Walid al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Makhzumi narrated to us, he said: Usama ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Silan, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Five the muhrim kills: the scorpion, the mouse, the kite, the vicious dog, and the snake. And this hadith has been narrated from Abu Hurayra from another angle, saying: the crow, without mentioning the snake or the serpent. And we do not know Ibn Silan narrated musnad from Abu Hurayra except these two hadiths, and he narrated another hadith mawquf."
"8184","Sulayman ibn Ubaydullah al-Ghaylani narrated it to us, he said: Abu Amir Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Silan, from Abu Hurayra, regarding the saying of Allah, Blessed and Exalted: {Fled from a lion}: he said: the lion."
"8185","Awf ibn al-Harith, from Abu Hurayra: Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Tahla', from Mihsan ibn Ali, from Awf ibn al-Harith, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever performs ablution well, then goes and finds people have prayed, Allah gives him like the reward of whoever prayed it and attended it, without decreasing anything from their rewards. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this angle with this chain."
"8186","Hajjaj ibn Hajjaj, from Abu Hurayra: Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Abd al-Hamid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ibrahim ibn Uqba, from Hajjaj ibn Hajjaj, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One or two sucks of breastfeeding do not prohibit, and nothing of it prohibits except what opens the intestines. And this hadith with this wording, we do not know it narrated except with this chain. And Hajjaj ibn Hajjaj was narrated from by Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, and he is known; he narrated from Abu Hurayra and from his father."
"8187","Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayra: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seven in the shade of the Throne, Allah shades them on a day when there is no shade except His shade: a just imam, a youth raised in worship of Allah, a man who remembered Allah alone and his eyes overflowed from fear of Allah, a man whom a woman of rank and wealth invited and he said: I fear Allah, a man who gave charity and concealed it so that his left hand does not know what his right hand made, or what his right hand spends, a man whose heart is attached to the mosques, or to the mosque, when he leaves it until he returns to it, and two men who loved each other for Allah, gathered upon that and parted. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from this angle with this chain."
"8188","Rizqullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed faith retreats to Madinah as the snake retreats to its hole."
"8189","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama narrated it to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Numayr and Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, they said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"8190","Rizqullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayra: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two garments and two sales, and prayer in two hours: after Asr until the sun sets, and after Fajr until the sun rises; and wrapping in one garment, and sitting with knees drawn up in a single garment exposing his private part to the sky; and munabadha and mulamasa."
"8191","Ubayd ibn Isma'il al-Habbari narrated to us, he said: Abu Usama narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Sayhan and Jayhan and the Nile and the Euphrates, each is from the rivers of Paradise."
"8192","Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karama narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Numayr and Abu Usama narrated to us, they said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Sayhan and Jayhan and the Nile and the Euphrates, each is from the rivers of Paradise."
"8193","Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Abu Usama narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: What is between my house and my minbar is a garden of the gardens of Paradise, and my minbar is upon my Hawd."
"8194","Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Khubayb, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: What is between my house and my minbar is a garden of the gardens of Paradise."
"8195","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Cool down the Zuhr prayer, for severe heat is from the blast of Hell. And this hadith, we do not recall it from the hadith of Ubaydullah, from Khubayb, except from Abd al-Wahhab."
"8196","Abdullah ibn Sa'id Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj al-Kindi narrated to us, he said: Uqba ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Euphrates is about to recede from a treasure of gold; whoever finds it, let him take nothing of it. Ubaydullah said: And Abu al-Zinad narrated to me, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayra, that he said: from a mountain of gold. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Ubaydullah except Uqba ibn Khalid."
"8197","Zayd ibn Akhzam Abu Talib narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Khubayb, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayra, and from Ubaydullah, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra, one of them raised it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, accepts charity and accepts of it only the pure, then nurtures it as one of you raises his foal or his young camel. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Ubaydullah except Jarir ibn Hazim."
"8198","Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Hassan ibn Hilal narrated to us, he said: Mubarak ibn Fadala narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Khubayb, from Hafs, from Abu Hurayra - he raised it."
"8199","Isma'il ibn Ibrahim, keeper of al-Quhi, narrated it to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Mubarak ibn Fadala, from Ubaydullah, from Khubayb, from Hafs, from Abu Hurayra, he raised it, he said: When Allah, Blessed and Exalted, created Adam, he sneezed and said: Praise be to Allah. So his Lord, Blessed and Exalted, said to him: May your Lord have mercy on you, O Adam. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Ubaydullah except Mubarak ibn Fadala."
"8200","Sulayman ibn Ubaydullah al-Ghaylani narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar, brother of Ubaydullah, narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Indeed Madinah, upon its passes are guards - I think he said - of angels; neither plague nor the Dajjal enters it."
"8201","Sulayman ibn Ubaydullah narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayra: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of pebbles. Meaning: when he throws the pebble the sale becomes binding; this was among the sales of Jahiliyyah, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade it. Likewise the sales of mulamasa and munabadha were sales the people of Jahiliyyah traded in, so the Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them. Mulamasa is that a man touches the garment then buys it before looking at it, and munabadha is that a man throws the garment to a man saying: when I throw it to you it is a sale from me to you. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that, since this throwing did not constitute a sale nor a valid transfer to him."
"8202","Al-Abbas ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Athma narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Khubayb, from Hafs, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A time will soon come upon people when the best of them is in a small flock of sheep, establishing prayer, giving zakat, and worshipping Allah until certainty comes to him."
"8203","Al-Abbas ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Athma narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Khubayb, from Hafs, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man may work, or he said: the worker works with the deeds of the people of Fire for seventy years, then his end is sealed with the deeds of the people of Paradise; and the worker works for seventy years with the deeds of the people of Paradise, then his end is sealed with the deeds of the people of Fire."
"8204","Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Khubayb, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Sayhun and Jayhun and the Nile and the Euphrates, each is from the rivers of Paradise, and each I have seen and drunk from. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Shu'ba, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs, from Abu Hurayra, except Yahya ibn Kathir."
"8205","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abbad Abu Abbad narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is between my grave and my minbar is a garden of the gardens of Paradise, and my minbar is upon a canal of the canals of Paradise. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Shu'ba except Yahya ibn Abbad Abu Abbad."
"8206","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, thus he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sufficient as a lie for a man is to narrate all he hears. And this hadith, Wahb sent it mursal, and Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated it musnad from Shu'ba, from Khubayb, from Hafs, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8207","Abda ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed us, from Musa ibn Ubayda, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayra, he said: I reviled fever in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he said: It surely removes the sins of the believer as the bellows removes the dross of iron. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Hafs except Alqama ibn Marthad, and we do not know it narrated from Alqama, from Hafs, except this hadith."
"8208","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayra: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What is between my house and my minbar is a garden of the gardens of Paradise."
"8209","Abu Bakr ibn Nafi' narrated it to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn al-Ala' narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Khubayb ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: What is between my house and my minbar is a garden of the gardens of Paradise, and a prayer in my mosque is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere except the Sacred Mosque."
"8210","Abu Ubayd, freed slave of Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar, from Abu Hurayra: al-Hasan ibn Qaza'a narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Ubayd, freed slave of Abd al-Rahman ibn Azhar, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: One of you will continue to be answered so long as he does not hasten."
"8211","Al-Hasan ibn Qaza'a narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Numayr narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Ubayd, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: That one of you gather a bundle of firewood and put it on his back is better for him than coming to a man and asking him, whether he gives him or withholds from him."
"8212","Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Ubayd, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you wish for death due to harm that befell him; let him say: O Allah, keep me alive so long as life is better for me, and take me when death is better for me."
"8213","Abbad ibn Aws, from Abu Hurayra: Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from Abbad ibn Aws, he said: Abu Hurayra narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Congregational prayer exceeds a man's prayer alone by twenty-five degrees. And we do not know Abbad ibn Aws narrated from Abu Hurayra except this hadith."
"8214","Busr ibn Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra: Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abu Alqama al-Farawi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Khusayfa narrated to us, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Any woman who touches incense, let her not attend prayer with us."
"8215","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, from al-Layth, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you will be saved by his deed. A man said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even I, except that Allah envelops me with mercy from Him."
"8216","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata' ibn Yasar and Busr ibn Sa'id and Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever catches a rak'a of Asr before the sun sets has caught it, and whoever catches a rak'a of Fajr before the sun rises has caught it."
"8217","Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Zayd, from Ata' ibn Yasar and Busr ibn Sa'id and Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"8218","Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari and Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, they said: Asbagh ibn al-Faraj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Bukayr ibn al-Ashajj, from Busr ibn Sa'id and Sulayman al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When it is a hot day, cool down the prayer, for severe heat is from the blast of Hell."
"8219","What Sa'id ibn Yasar narrated from Abu Hurayra: Muhammad ibn Bashshar ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Musa ibn Abi Tamim, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dinar for dinar and dirham for dirham, no excess between them. And this hadith was narrated by Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, from Musa ibn Abi Tamim, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8220","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Sa'sa'a, who is Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sa'sa'a, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever Allah wills good for, He afflicts him. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayra except from this angle."
"8221","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talha, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from poverty, and from littleness and humiliation, and I seek refuge in You from wronging or being wronged."
"8222","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Rawh narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, he said: He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no commander of ten except he will be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hands chained to his neck; the truth will free him or ruin him."
"8223","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubada narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to a town that consumes towns; they say Yathrib, and it is Madinah; it expels people as the bellows expels the dross of iron. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Abu Hurayra with this chain."
"8224","Rizqullah ibn Musa Abu al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Shababa ibn Sawwar narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata', from Sa'id ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Angels attend - meaning the dead person. When the righteous man is there, he says: Come out, O good soul that was in the good body; come out praiseworthy and receive glad tidings of rest and sweet basil and a Lord not angry. It continues to be said to it until it comes out, then it is taken up to heaven and admission is sought for it. It is said: Who is this? They say: So-and-so. They say: Welcome to the good soul that was in the good body; enter praiseworthy. It continues to be said to it until it is brought to Allah, Blessed and Exalted. And when the evil man is there, he says: Come out, O wicked soul that was in the wicked body; come out blameworthy and receive tidings of boiling water and pus and other kinds of its like. He said: So it comes out, then it is taken up to heaven and admission is sought for it. It is said: So-and-so; they say: No welcome to the wicked soul that was in the wicked body; return blameworthy, for the gates of heaven will not be opened for you. Then he goes to the grave. The righteous man is seated in his grave neither frightened nor terrified; it is said to him: In what were you? He says: In Islam. It is said to him: What do you say about this man? He says: He is the Messenger of Allah; he came to us with clear proofs from our Lord, so we believed in him and confirmed him. It is said to him: Did you see Allah? He says: It is not for anyone to see Allah. An opening is made for him toward the Fire and he looks at it, part crushing part. It is said: Look at what Allah protected you from. Then an opening is made for him to Paradise and he looks at its blossom and what is in it. It is said to him: This is what Allah prepared for you. And it is said to him: Upon certainty you lived and upon it you died, and upon it you will be raised, if Allah wills. And the evil man is seated in his grave frightened and terrified; it is said to him: In what were you? He says: I do not know. It is said: What did you say about this man? He says: I do not know; I heard people saying something. An opening is made for him toward Paradise and he looks at its blossom and what is in it; it is said: Look at what Allah diverted from you. Then an opening is made for him toward the Fire and he looks at it, part crushing part; it is said: This is your seat and abode; upon doubt you lived and upon it you died, then he is punished. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except from this angle with this chain."
"8225","Abd al-Malik ibn Isa, from Abu Hurayra: Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Muti' al-Husayn ibn Abdullah al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmala narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Isa, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Learn of your lineages what you join your kinship with; for joining kinship extends life and increases wealth. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except from this angle with this chain."
"8226","Hanzala ibn Ali, from Abu Hurayra: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami narrated to us, he said: Ma'n ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: I heard Hanzala ibn Ali, he said: Abu Hurayra narrated to us, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The grateful eater is like the patient fasting person. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayra except with this chain, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Hanzala ibn Ali except Ma'n ibn Muhammad, and Ma'n ibn Jurayj narrated it from Ma'n."
"8227","Abu Ghassan Rawh ibn Hatim narrated it to us, he said: Shihab ibn Abbad narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ma'n ibn Muhammad, from Hanzala ibn Ali, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"8228","Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami narrated to us, he said: Ma'n ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Hanzala ibn Ali, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Every deed of the son of Adam is for him except fasting, for it is Mine and I reward for it; he leaves food and drink for My sake. This hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Hanzala ibn Ali except Ma'n ibn Muhammad, nor from Ma'n except Umar ibn Ali."
"8229","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from al-Zuhri, from Hanzala ibn Ali, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8230","Husayn ibn al-Lajlaj from Abu Hurayra: al-Hasan ibn Arafa narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Abbad al-Muhallabi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Safwan ibn Abi Yazid, from Husayn ibn al-Lajlaj, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Miserliness and faith do not combine in the belly of a Muslim man, nor do dust in the path of Allah and smoke of Hell combine in the belly of a Muslim man. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayra except from this angle."
"8231","Abdullah ibn Rafi', from Abu Hurayra: Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ubayda narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Khalid, from Abdullah ibn Rafi', from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There will come with me of my ummah on the Day of Resurrection like the flood and the night, then a crushing multitude; the angels will say: What came with Muhammad is more than what came with the rest of the nations, or the prophets. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this angle."
"8232","One of our companions, Ubaydullah ibn Sa'id or another, narrated to us, from Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim, he said: My father narrated to me, from Ibn Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Rafi', from Abu Hurayra, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah, Blessed and Exalted, willed to confine Yunus in the belly of the whale, Allah revealed to the whale: Do not scratch for him flesh nor break for him bone. So it took him then descended with him to its dwelling in the sea. When it reached with him the bottom of the sea, Yunus heard a sound; he said to himself: What is this? So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, revealed to him while he was in the belly of the whale that this is the glorification of the creatures of the earth. So he glorified while in the belly of the whale; the angels heard his glorification and said: Our Lord, we hear a faint voice in a strange land. He, Blessed and Exalted, said: That is My servant Yunus; he disobeyed Me, so I confined him in the belly of the whale in the sea. They said: The righteous servant from whom a righteous deed used to ascend to You every day and night? He said: Yes. So they interceded for him thereupon, and He commanded the whale and it cast him upon the shore, as Allah, Blessed and Exalted, said: {While he was sick}. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with this wording except from this angle with this chain."
"8233","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Mukharrimi and al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani and al-Abbas ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, they said: al-Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Isma'il ibn Umayya, from Ayyub ibn Khalid, from Abdullah ibn Rafi', from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand and said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, created the soil on Saturday, created in it the mountains on Sunday, created trees on Monday, created the disliked on Tuesday, created light on Wednesday, and spread - I think he said - in it creatures on Thursday, and created Adam after Asr on Friday, the last of creation in the last hour of the hours of Friday, between Asr and night. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"8234","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Aflah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Rafi', from Abu Hurayra, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If your life is prolonged, you will soon see people going out in Allah's anger and returning in Allah's curse, in their hands like the tails of cattle. And this hadith, we do not know anyone narrated it from Abdullah ibn Rafi' except Aflah ibn Sa'id, and he is a well-known man of the people of Quba."
"8235","Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Attab narrated to us, reciting from me to him, he said: Abu Ayyub Sulayman ibn Khalaf narrated to us, he said: Abu Abdullah Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Mufarrij narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Habib al-Raqqi informed us, he said: Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Tulayq ibn Muhammad al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, he said: Musa ibn Yasar narrated to us, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wakes, let him not put his hand into the washing, or he said into the water, until he washes it three times; for he does not know where his hand spent the night."
"8236","Tulayq ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, and from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayra: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wisal; they said: You practice wisal. He said: In that I am not like you; indeed Allah, Blessed and Exalted, feeds me and gives me drink. So take on of deeds what you have capacity for."
"8237","Tulayq narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever obeys me has obeyed Allah, and whoever obeys my commander has obeyed me; and whoever disobeys me has disobeyed Allah, and whoever disobeys my commander has disobeyed me."
"8238","Tulayq ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My likeness and the likeness of the prophets before me is like a man who built a house and perfected and beautified it except the place of a brick; people began circling it, marveling at it, saying: We never saw better than this, were it not for the place of this brick. So I was the place of that brick."
"8239","Tulayq ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, as far as I know: If I had like Uhud in gold, it would please me to spend it in the path of Allah, with no third night coming upon me while I have of it a dinar or dirham, except something I set aside for a debt upon me."
"8240","Tulayq ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting is a shield; when one of you is fasting, let him not speak obscenely nor act ignorantly. And if a man insults him, let him say: I am a fasting man."
"8241","Tulayq ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The changed breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter with Allah than the scent of musk."
"8242","Tulayq ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, I think in what he narrates from his Lord: Every deed of the son of Adam is for him except fasting; it is Mine and I reward for it. The good deed is ten like it up to seven hundred multiples except fasting; it is Mine and I reward for it."
"8243","Tulayq narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The poor one is not he whom a date or two dates turn away; rather the poor one is he who does not ask people nor is noticed so he is given."
"8244","Tulayq ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that I would burden my ummah, I would not have stayed behind a detachment raiding in the path of Allah; but I do not find means to carry them, nor do they find means to follow me, nor are their souls content to stay behind."
"8245","Muhammad ibn Harb al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile time, for Allah is Time; He alternates night and day, and brings the ages."
"8246","Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The barren animal is without liability, the well is without liability, the mine is without liability, and in buried treasure is the fifth."
"8247","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Delaying payment by the rich is injustice."
"8248","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Severe heat is from the blast of Hell, so cool down the prayer."
"8249","Al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf, known as Ibn al-Sha'ir, narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Ishaq, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he saw a man driving a sacrificial camel; he said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial camel! He said: Ride it."
"8250","Ibrahim ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Abu Tumayla narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not wish to meet the enemy; for you do not know what will be in that."
"8251","Abda ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir informed us, he said: Abdullah ibn Sulayman ibn Abdullah ibn Hanzala narrated to us, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No one leaves Madinah except Allah replaces him with one better than him."
"8252","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Yasar narrated to me, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes my name, let him not take my kunya, for I am Abu al-Qasim."
"8253","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever buys a musarra, let him milk it; if he is pleased with it, otherwise let him return it with a sa' of dates."
"8254","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The changed breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter with Allah than the scent of musk."
"8255","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Qays narrated to us, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, he said: Our dowry when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among us was ten uqiyas."
"8256","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is surely more joyful at the repentance of His servant than one of you - I think he said - finding his lost item, I think he said - in a desert land with his food and drink upon it."
"8257","Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Musa ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Day angels succeed night angels, and they gather in the dawn prayer and Asr prayer. Those who were among you ascend, and He, Blessed and Exalted, says: How did you leave My servants? They say: We came to them while they prayed and left them while they prayed."
"8258","Nafi' ibn Sarjis, from Abu Hurayra: Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Ali al-Ju'fi narrated to us, he said: Za'ida narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Nafi' ibn Sarjis, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In the end of time there will be tribulations like pieces of dark night; the safest of people from them is the owner of a mountain peak who eats from the produce of his sheep, or from the flock of his sheep, and a man holding his horse's bridle who eats from the spoils of his horse or his spear. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayra except from this angle with this chain, and we do not know Nafi' ibn Sarjis narrated musnad from Abu Hurayra except this hadith."
"8259","Ubayd, freed slave of Abu Ruhm, from Abu Hurayra: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Ubayd, freed slave of Abu Ruhm, from Abu Hurayra: that a woman passed by him and he smelled perfume oil from her. Abu Hurayra said to her: Do you intend the mosque? She said: Yes. He said: And did you perfume yourself for it? She said: Yes. So Abu Hurayra said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman who perfumes herself then comes to the mosque, her prayer is not accepted until she washes as she washes from janaba. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayra except from two angles, this is one of them, and we do not know anyone narrated it from Ubayd except Asim."
"8260","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated it to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Ubayd, freed slave of Abu Ruhm, from Abu Hurayra, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah does not accept the prayer of a woman who perfumes herself for the mosque, or for this mosque, until she washes as she washes from janaba."
"8261","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Ubayd, freed slave of Abu Ruhm, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I guide you to a treasure of the treasures of Paradise? There is no might nor power except with Allah."
"8262","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Ubayd, freed slave of Abu Ruhm, from Abu Hurayra, he said: I was with him and he passed by an open space and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Many an oath does not ascend to Allah in this spot. He said: So I saw the slave-traders in it thereafter. And this hadith, we do not know a path for it from Abu Hurayra except this path."
"8263","Abida ibn Sufyan al-Hadrami from him: Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Hakim, from Abida ibn Sufyan al-Hadrami, from Abu Hurayra, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Eating every predator with fangs is forbidden. And we do not know Abida narrated musnad from Abu Hurayra except this hadith."
"8264","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from Abu Hurayra: Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khusayfa, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, and I know it only from Abu Hurayra, he said: A thief was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); they said: He stole. He said: I do not think he stole. He said: Yes, I did, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Take him and cut him, then cauterize him, then bring him to me. So he was taken, cut, then cauterized, then brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: Repent to Allah. He said: I repent to Allah. He said: May Allah accept your repentance, or he said: O Allah, accept his repentance. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayra except from this angle with this chain."
"8265","Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khusayfa, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban - and I do not know whether he mentioned it from Abu Hurayra or not, and I have seen one who mentions it from Abu Hurayra, though I do not recall it from Abu Hurayra - he said: When you see a man selling in the mosque, say: May Allah not profit your trade; and when you see one announcing a lost item in the mosque, say: May Allah not return your lost item to you. And this hadith, if it were established from Abu Hurayra, there would be no path recalled for it from Abu Hurayra other than this path."
"8266","8261 - Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Abu Hisham al-Mughirah ibn Salamah al-Makhzumi narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated, from Abu Waqid, from Ishaq the freedman of Za'idah, and Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever washes a dead body, let him perform ghusl, and whoever carries him, let him perform wudu. I heard Abu Musa Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna say: I heard Bishr ibn Umar say: I asked Malik ibn Anas about Salih the freedman of al-Taw'amah, and he said: He is not trustworthy."
"8267","Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi', from Abu Hurayrah. 8262 - Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Ibn Abi Rafi', that Abu Hurayrah prayed the Friday prayer and recited Surah al-Jumu'ah and (When the hypocrites come to you). He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite them both on Friday. And we do not know that Ubaydullah ibn Abi Rafi' narrated as musnad from Abu Hurayrah except this hadith."
"8268","Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Hurayrah. 8263 - Rizqullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ma'n ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the children of the polytheists, and he said: Allah knows best what they would have done. And this hadith has been narrated by more than one from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid."
"8269","8264 - Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Ubaydullah narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid and Abu Abdillah al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, descends every night when the last third of the night remains to the lowest heaven and says: Who supplicates to Me so I may answer him? Who seeks My forgiveness so I may forgive him? Who asks Me so I may give him? Until the dawn rises. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, except Salih; rather the trustworthy memorizers narrate it from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah and al-Agharr."
"8270","8265 - Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id, that the people said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Will we see our Lord on the Day of Resurrection? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you dispute about the moon on the night of full moon when there is no cloud below it? They said: No. He said: Do you dispute about seeing the sun when there is no cloud below it? They said: No. He said: Then you will see Him likewise. People will be detained on the Day of Resurrection, then it will be said: Whoever used to worship something, let him follow it. Some will follow the sun, some will follow the moon, and some will follow the false gods, and this ummah will remain with its hypocrites among it until He, Blessed and Exalted, comes to them and says: I am your Lord. They will say: You are our Lord. Then Allah will strike across the midst of Hell, and I will be the first of the Messengers to cross with my ummah, and none will speak that day except the Messengers, and the supplication of the Messengers that day will be: O Allah, grant safety, grant safety. And in Hell are hooks like the thorns of al-Sa'dan. Have you seen the thorns of al-Sa'dan? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: They are like the thorns of al-Sa'dan, snatching people by their deeds; some will be scratched down, and some will be saved, until when Allah, Blessed and Exalted, intends mercy for whom He wills among the people of the Fire, Allah commands that whoever used to worship Allah be brought out, so they bring them out, recognizing them by the trace of prostration, for Allah has forbidden the Fire to consume the trace of prostration. They come out of the Fire having been scorched, then the water of life is poured over them, and they grow in it as the seed grows in the silt of the flood. Then Allah, Blessed and Exalted, finishes judging between the servants, and there remains a man between Paradise and Hell, the last of the people of Paradise to enter Paradise, facing the Fire. He says: O my Lord, turn my face away from the Fire, for its wind has poisoned me and its flame has burned me. Allah, Blessed and Exalted, says: Perhaps if I do that for you, you will ask Me for something else? He says: No, by Your might. He gives his Lord whatever covenant and pledge He wills, so Allah turns his face from the Fire. When he faces Paradise and sees its splendor, he remains silent as long as Allah wills him to remain silent, then says: O my Lord, bring me forward to the gate of Paradise. Allah says: Did you not give the covenants and pledges that you would not ask for other than what you asked? He says: O my Lord, let me not be the most wretched of Your creation. He says: Perhaps if I grant you that, you will ask Me for something else? He says: No, by Your might, I will not ask You for other than that. He gives his Lord whatever covenant and pledge He wills, so He brings him forward to the gate of Paradise. When he reaches its gate and it opens for him, and he sees its blossom and the freshness and joy within, he remains silent as long as Allah wills, then says: O my Lord, admit me into Paradise. He, Blessed and Exalted, says: How treacherous you are! You gave the covenants and pledges that you would not ask for other than what you were given. He says: O my Lord, do not make me the most wretched of Your creation. So Allah, Blessed and Exalted, laughs at him, then permits him to enter Paradise, then says: Wish. When his wishes are exhausted, Allah says to him, and his Lord reminds him, until when his wishes end, Allah says to him: Yours is that and the like of it with it. Abu Sa'id al-Khudri said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yours is that and ten times its like. Abu Hurayrah said: I only memorized from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Yours is that and the like of it with it. Abu Sa'id said: I bear witness that I heard him say: Yours is that and ten times its like. And this hadith was narrated by Shu'ayb and Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab and Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id."
"8271","8266 - Ahmad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, as far as I know, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Abu Ubayd, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever glorifies Allah after a prayer thirty-three times, praises thirty-three times, and magnifies thirty-three times, and says to complete one hundred: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things capable, his sins are forgiven even if they are more than the foam of the sea. And Abu Ubayd from whom Suhayl narrated this hadith, we do not know who he is."
"8272","Salman al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah. 8267 - Abu Hisham Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Rifa'i narrated to us: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Habib and Abu Ishaq, from al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a third of the night has gone, or the middle of the night, or He waits until a third of the night, or until the middle of the night, He commands a caller who calls: Is there any supplicant so I may answer him? Is there any seeker of forgiveness so he may be forgiven? Is there any asker so he may be given? Is there any repentant one so he may be turned to?"
"8273","8268 - Ma'mar ibn Sahl narrated it to us, he said: Muhadir narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq and Habib, from al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"8274","8269 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar and Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Agharr who said: I bear witness regarding Abu Sa'id and Abu Hurayrah that they both bore witness regarding the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"8275","8270 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated it to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Agharr, from Abu Muslim who said: I bear witness regarding Abu Sa'id and Abu Hurayrah that they both bore witness regarding the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, waits until when a third of the night has gone, or remained, He descends and says: Is there any supplicant who will be answered - I think he said: Is there any asker who will be given, any seeker of forgiveness for a sin."
"8276","8271 - Ahmad ibn Mansur ibn Sayyar narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from al-A'mash, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Agharr, that he narrated to him, from Abu Sa'id and Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, raising it: Might is My lower garment and pride is My upper garment; whoever contends with Me for anything of them, I will punish him. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Hafs, nor from Hafs except Umar ibn Hafs."
"8277","8272 - Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Agharr Abu Muslim who said: I bear witness regarding Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id that they both bore witness regarding the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: No people sit remembering Allah except the angels surround them, mercy covers them, and Allah mentions them among those with Him."
"8278","8273 - Ubaydullah ibn Yusuf al-Jubayri narrated to us, he said: al-Aghlab ibn Tamim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: When the servant says: There is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, his Lord confirms him, saying: My servant has spoken truth; there is no god but Me, and I am Greatest. When the servant says: There is no god but Allah alone, his Lord confirms him, saying: There is no god but Me alone. When the servant says: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, his Lord confirms him, saying: There is no god but Me alone without partner. When the servant says: There is no god but Allah alone without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, his Lord confirms him, saying: There is no god but Me alone without partner; to Me belongs dominion and to Me belongs praise. When the servant says: There is no god but Allah, and there is no power nor strength except through Allah, his Lord confirms him, saying: There is no god but Me, and there is no power nor strength except through Me. And this hadith has been narrated from Abu Ishaq, from al-Agharr, by more than one."
"8279","8274 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Salman al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in what he relates from his Lord, Blessed and Exalted, who said: Whoever remembers Me within himself, I remember him within Myself, and whoever remembers Me in a gathering of people, I remember him in a greater and better gathering than them."
"8280","8275 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Hafs narrated to me, from al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perform wudu from what fire has cooked. And we do not know that Abu Bakr ibn Hafs narrated from al-Agharr except this hadith."
"8281","8276 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us - as I think, or another of Shu'bah's companions - from Shu'bah, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, from al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere among the mosques, except the Sacred Mosque."
"8282","8277 - Abd al-Quddus ibn Abd al-Kabir narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Maslamah narrated to us, he said: Aflah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Salman al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Congregational prayer equals twenty-five of the prayer of the lone person, and a prayer in this mosque of mine is like a thousand prayers elsewhere among the mosques except the Sacred Mosque - I think he said: And no one endures its hardship and severity - meaning Madinah - except I will be his intercessor and witness on the Day of Resurrection."
"8283","8278 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Salman al-Agharr, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not fitting for a two-faced person to be trustworthy."
"8284","8279 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Salman al-Agharr narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere among the mosques except the Sacred Mosque."
"8285","8280 - Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Salman al-Agharr narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you walk in a single sandal; let him take them both off or wear them both."
"8286","8281 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from al-Agharr Abu Muslim, from Abu Hurayrah and Abu Sa'id who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you wakes in the night and wakes his family and they both pray together, they are recorded among the men who remember Allah much and the women who remember. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Agharr except Ali ibn al-Aqmar, nor from al-A'mash except Shayban; al-Thawri narrated it from Ali ibn al-Aqmar without raising it, except Abd al-Razzaq from al-Thawri."
"8287","8282 - Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Ubaydullah ibn Salman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, sends a wind from Yemen softer than silk, and it leaves no one in whose heart is a speck of faith except it takes him. And we do not know this hadith narrated except from Abu Hurayrah with this chain."
"8288","8283 - Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Musa ibn Uqbah who said: Ubaydullah ibn Salman narrated to me, from his father, that he heard Abu Hurayrah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never left the Duha prayer, neither in travel nor otherwise."
"8289","8284 - Khalid narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ubaydullah ibn Salman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays at night with one hundred verses is not recorded among the heedless, and whoever prays with two hundred verses is recorded - I think he said - among the God-fearing."
"8290","8285 - Khalid ibn Yusuf, meaning Ibn Khalid, narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Musa ibn Uqbah who said: Ubaydullah ibn Salman narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The farther, so the farther of you has the greater reward, meaning in the distance of steps to the mosque. And we do not know these hadiths narrated from Abu Hurayrah except from this angle with this chain, and we do not know anyone who narrated them from Musa except Yusuf ibn Khalid; and Yusuf ibn Khalid was a man who had written hadith, traveling with it to Kufah, writing from al-A'mash, and he was the first to compose extended books on legal documents. But he entered into theological disputation and exceeded the bounds of the people of knowledge, so his hadith was weakened because of that."
"8291","Abu Abdillah al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah. 8286 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Mujammi' narrated to us, he said: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Abu Abdillah al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah rejoices at the repentance of His servant more intensely than one of you with his camel in a deadly land, fearing thirst will kill him there. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from al-Agharr, except Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Mujammi', and Ibn Mujammi' was not followed on this chain."
"8292","8287 - Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us, he said: Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid and Abu Abdillah al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [The matn is not stated here beyond the chain.]"
"8293","8288 - Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from al-Zuhri, from al-Agharr and Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, descends every night to the lowest heaven when the last third of the night remains, saying: Who supplicates to Me so I may answer him? Who asks Me so I may give him? Who seeks My forgiveness so I may forgive him?"
"8294","8289 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, as I think, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abu Abdillah the freedman of Juhaynah, namely al-Agharr, narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere except the Sacred Mosque."
"8295","8290 - al-Abbas narrated to us, he said: Atiq ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Qudamah al-Jumahi narrated to us, from Abu Abdillah al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when rain befell them in Madinah and the spouts flowed, would say: There is no harm upon them this year."
"8296","8291 - al-Abbas ibn Ubayy narrated to us, he said: Atiq ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Qudamah narrated to us, from Abu Abdillah al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to trim his nails and cut his mustache on Friday before going out to prayer. And we do not know anyone who narrated these two hadiths from Abu Abdillah al-Agharr except Ibrahim ibn Qudamah, and he was not followed on them, because these two hadiths are not narrated from Abu Hurayrah from any angle except this one; and when Ibrahim ibn Qudamah is alone with a hadith, he is not a proof, for he is not well-known, even if he is among the people of Madinah."
"8297","8292 - Abu Kamil narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: There is no god but Allah, it will benefit him one day of his lifetime, though he will be afflicted before that with whatever afflicts him. And we do not know this hadith narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except from this angle with this chain; Isa ibn Yunus narrated it from al-Thawri, from Mansur as well, following him in this narration. Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated this hadith from Hilal ibn Yasaf and al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah, as mawquf; and Mansur is more retentive than Husayn."
"8298","8293 - Zayd ibn Akhzam and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar, as I think, narrated to us, they said: Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Nu'man narrating from al-Zuhri, from Abu Abdillah al-Agharr the freedman of Juhaynah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When it is Friday - I think he said: There are angels at the doors of the mosque writing the people, whoever comes first, first; when the imam comes out, the scrolls are folded and they come to listen to the remembrance."
"8299","8294 - Zayd ibn Akhzam, or Muhammad ibn Ma'mar, narrated to us, he said: Wahb narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Nu'man narrating from al-Zuhri, from Abu Abdillah al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The likeness of one who hastens early to Friday is like one who offers a camel, the next offers a cow, the next is like one offering a ram, the next is like one offering a chicken, the next is like one offering an egg. And we do not know anyone who narrated these two hadiths from al-Zuhri, from al-Agharr, except al-Nu'man; others than al-Nu'man narrated them from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id, from Abu Hurayrah."
"8300","Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'qub, from Abu Hurayrah. 8295 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: Two people who revile each other: what they say is upon the one who began, until the wronged one transgresses. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurayrah except from this angle."
"8301","8296 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Rights will surely be restored to their owners on the Day of Resurrection, even the hornless sheep avenged by its goring. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurayrah except from this angle."
"8302","8297 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Every prayer in which the Mother of the Qur'an is not recited is deficient. There is disagreement about this hadith: Malik narrated it from al-Ala, from Abu al-Sa'ib the freedman of Hisham, from Abu Hurayrah; Shu'bah narrated it from al-Ala, from his father; and Abu Uways narrated it from al-Ala, from his father and Abu al-Sa'ib, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8303","8298 - Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The world is the prison of the believer and the paradise of the disbeliever. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurayrah except from this angle with this chain."
"8304","8299 - Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Kathir narrated to us, and we found these hadiths written in my handwriting from him, he said: Ibn Ulayyah narrated to us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about backbiting and said: Mentioning your brother with what he dislikes. He said: What if what I say is in my brother? He said: If what you say is in him, you have backbitten him; if it is not in him, you have slandered him."
"8305","8300 - And I found in my book, from Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim who said: Isma'il Ibn Ulayyah informed us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the graveyard and said: Peace upon the abode of a believing people; he greeted its people and said: We, if Allah wills, will join you. I wish we had seen our brothers. They said: Are we not your brothers? He said: You are my companions, and my brothers are a people who come after me from my ummah, and I am their forerunner at the Pond. They said: How will you recognize those of your ummah who have not yet come? He said: Tell me, if a man had horses with white blazes and white feet among jet-black horses, would he not recognize his horses? They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: They will come with white blazes and white marks from the traces of wudu, and I am your forerunner at the Pond; and I will drive men away from my Pond as a camel is driven away, saying: Come forth! Then it will be said: They innovated after you, so I will say: Away, away."
"8306","8301 - And I found in my book, from Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim who said: Isma'il informed us, from Rawh ibn al-Qasim, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - I think he raised it - who said: I am the most self-sufficient of partners from partnership; whoever does a deed for Me associating another with Me in it - he mentioned a word, I think he said: It belongs to My partner."
"8307","8302 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad informed us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I have been commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah. When they bear witness that there is no god but Allah and believe in me and in what I came with, they protect - I think he said: From me - their blood except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah."
"8308","8303 - Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad informed us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, and Suhayl ibn Abi Salih from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best rows of men are the first, and the worst are the last; the best rows of women are the last, and the worst are the first."
"8309","8304 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Madinah expels its wicked people."
"8310","8305 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: A man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): My father died leaving wealth without bequeathing; will it expiate for him if I give charity on his behalf? He said: Yes."
"8311","8306 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrating from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not point you to what Allah raises ranks by and removes sins by: many steps to the mosque, waiting for prayer after prayer, and performing wudu fully despite hardships."
"8312","8307 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrating from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer - twice or thrice - feels jealousy, and Allah feels jealousy, and Allah is more jealous."
"8313","8308 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you supplicates, let him not say: If You will; rather let him be firm."
"8314","8309 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrating from his Lord, Blessed and Exalted, who said: I am the best of partners; whoever does a deed associating another with Me in it, I am free of it, and it belongs to the one he associated."
"8315","8310 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Charity does not decrease wealth, and no man pardons a wrong except Allah increases him in honor, and no man humbles himself except Allah raises him."
"8316","8311 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): That he forbade vows and said: It does not turn back anything of the decree; rather it is extracted by it from the miser."
"8317","8312 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Let no man outbid his brother, nor propose over his engagement. Muhammad said: And Shu'bah narrated to us, from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it."
"8318","8313 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A false oath sells the goods but wipes out the blessing."
"8319","8314 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Do you know what backbiting is? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Your mentioning your brother. He said: Tell me, if what I say is in my brother? He said: If what you say is in him, you have backbitten him; if what you say is not in him, you have slandered him."
"8320","8315 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Qays narrated to us, he said: al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The signs of the hypocrite are three: when he speaks he lies, when he promises he breaks it, and when entrusted he betrays."
"8321","8316 - Isma'il ibn Abi Isma'il al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ya'qub, freedman of al-Huraqah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Help your brother whether oppressor or oppressed; if he is an oppressor, help against him until the right is taken from him, for you have helped him thereby; if he is oppressed, help him until he takes his right, for you have helped him."
"8322","8317 - Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man may act for a long time with the deeds of the people of Paradise, then his deeds are sealed with the deeds of the people of the Fire, so Allah makes him among the people of the Fire; and a man may act for a long time with the deeds of the people of the Fire, then Allah seals his deeds with the deeds of the people of Paradise, so Allah makes him among the people of Paradise."
"8323","8318 - al-Fadl ibn Isma'il and Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, they said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that a black man used to clean the mosque, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed him and they said: He died. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to his grave and prayed over him. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Ala except Muhammad ibn Abi Kathir."
"8324","8319 - Muhammad ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Abu Tawbah al-Rabi' ibn Nafi' narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Maysarah narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Charity never decreased wealth at all."
"8325","8320 - Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Qurashi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever cheats us is not of us."
"8326","8321 - Muhammad ibn Harb al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Rich, Allah Blessed and Exalted, says: I asked My servant for a loan and he did not lend Me, and he harms Me; he says: O woe to the age, and I am time."
"8327","8322 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he came to the graveyard and said: Peace be upon you, abode of a believing people, and we, if Allah wills, will join you. Then he said: I wish we had met our brothers. We said: O Messenger of Allah, are we not your brothers? He said: You are my companions, and my brothers are those who have not yet come after me, and I am their forerunner at the Pond. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how will you recognize those of your ummah who have not come? He said: Tell me, if a man had horses with white blazes and white feet among jet-black horses, would he not recognize them? They said: Yes. He said: They will come on the Day of Resurrection with white blazes and white marks from the traces of wudu, and I am their forerunner at the Pond - I think he said: I drive away from my Pond as the stray camel is driven away - then he mentioned a word - then it will be said: They changed after you; they kept turning back on their heels! So I will say: Away, away."
"8328","8323 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar Bundar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I have relatives I join while they cut me off, I do good to them while they do evil to me, I forbear toward them while they act ignorantly toward me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If it is as you say, it is as if you feed them hot ashes, and there will remain with you a supporter from Allah as long as you continue upon that. And we do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurayrah except through al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah."
"8329","8324 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - as I think he said: Upon every gate of the mosque on Friday are two angels writing the first, then the first, like a man who offered a camel, like a man who offered a cow, like a man who offered a bird, and like a man who offered an egg; when the imam sits, meaning upon the pulpit, the scrolls are folded."
"8330","8325 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Hour will not come until thirty impostors appear, each claiming he is the messenger of Allah, and until wealth overflows, tribulations appear, and harj increases. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is harj? He said: Killing, killing."
"8331","8326 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Ala, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Shall I not point you to what Allah raises ranks by and expiates sins by: many steps to the mosques, waiting for prayer after prayer, and performing wudu fully despite hardships."
"8332","8327 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as I think he said: When one of you supplicates - I think he said: Let him be firm, for nothing Allah gives is too great for Him."
"8333","8328 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Faith is Yemeni, and disbelief is toward the east."
"8334","8329 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade making nabidh in gourds and varnished vessels."
"8335","8330 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The sun does not rise on a day better than Friday - I think he said: And there is nothing except it fears Friday, except the two weighty beings, the jinn and mankind."
"8336","8331 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Abi al-Wazir narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: If the believer knew what punishment is with Allah, he would never hope for Paradise at all; and if the disbeliever knew what mercy is with Allah, he would never despair of mercy at all."
"8337","8332 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A disbeliever and his Muslim killer will never gather in the Fire."
"8338","8333 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever washes a bier, meaning a dead body, let him perform ghusl; and whoever carries it, let him perform wudu."
"8339","8334 - Umar ibn Hafs al-Shaybani narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever fasts Ramadan and follows it with six of Shawwal, it is as if he fasted the whole year. This hadith was narrated by Abu Amir from Zuhayr from al-Ala, and Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated it from Zuhayr from Suhayl, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah; and I did not hear anyone narrating it from Abu Amir except Umar ibn Hafs; I saw it in the book of Ahmad ibn Thabit written, and he said: Abu Amir did not read it to us."
"8340","8335 - Sadaqah ibn al-Fadl al-Ammi narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, he said: Mus'ab ibn Thabit narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met Hudhayfah and wanted to shake his hand, but Hudhayfah stepped aside and said to him: I am junub! He said: When a believer shakes the hand of his brother, their sins fall away as the leaves of a tree fall away."
"8341","8336 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the major sins is a man overreaching in the honor of a man, or a Muslim man, without right; and among the major sins are two insults answered by an insult."
"8342","8337 - Ahmad ibn al-Muqaddam al-Ijli narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The transgressing party will kill Ammar. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-Ala except Abdullah ibn Ja'far, nor is it narrated from Abu Hurayrah except from this angle."
"8343","8338 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever calls to guidance has a reward like the reward of whoever follows him, without decreasing anything from their rewards; and whoever calls to misguidance bears a sin like the sins of whoever follows him, without decreasing anything from their sins."
"8344","8339 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Muqaddami narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no disease except in black seed there is healing for it, except death."
"8345","8340 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Straighten the rows well in prayer."
"8346","Ajlan Abu Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah. 8341 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Bukayr ibn Abdillah ibn al-Ashajj, from Ajlan Abu Muhammad, from Abu Hurayrah - as a report - who said: The slave has his food and clothing, and he is not tasked of work except what he can bear."
"8347","8342 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best rows of men are the first, and the worst are the last in prayer; the best rows of women in prayer are the last, and the worst are the first. This hadith has been narrated by more than one from Ibn Ajlan, among them Sufyan al-Thawri, and Abu Nu'aym narrated it from him; it is a hadith well-known from Ibn Ajlan, and we do not know it narrated from Abu Hurayrah except from this angle."
"8348","8343 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most numerous are the least, except one who says like this and like this and like this."
"8349","8344 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have a neighbor who harms me. He said to him: Take out your goods and place them on the road. The man took his goods and threw them on the road, and everyone who passed by him said: What is wrong with you? He said: My neighbor harms me! So he says: O Allah, curse him; O Allah, disgrace him. Then the man said: Return to your home; by Allah, I will never harm you again. We do not know this hadith narrated from Abu Hurayrah except from this angle with this chain; and there has been narrated in this speech and its like from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) by Abu Hurayrah with this chain, and Abu Juhayfah Wahb ibn Abdillah narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Yusuf ibn Abdillah ibn Salam also narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"8350","8345 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: I slaughtered a sheep for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Hand me the foreleg. So I handed him the foreleg. Then he said: Hand me the foreleg. So I handed him the foreleg. Then he said: Hand me the foreleg. I said: O Messenger of Allah, a sheep has only two forelegs. He said: If you had searched, you would have found it."
"8351","8346 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with something similar."
"8352","8347 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from my father - from Abu Hurayrah - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of one who comes early to Friday is like one who offers a camel, then like one who offers a cow, then like one who offers a sheep, then like one who offers a chicken, then like one who offers a sparrow, then like one who offers an egg; when the imam comes out and sits upon the pulpit, the scrolls are folded."
"8353","8348 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave me as I have left you; those before you were destroyed only by their questioning and differing over their prophets. What I forbid you, refrain from; and what I command you, take from it what you can."
"8354","8349 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I intended that prayer be established, then I command a man to lead the people in prayer, then I go to people who do not attend prayer and burn it over them; and if a fat meaty bone or two arrow-targets were set for one of them, he would attend."
"8355","8350 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Safwan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The best of people are my generation, then those upon their heels, then those upon their heels."
"8356","8351 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Safwan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The best women who rode camels are the most tender to a child and the most careful with a husband in what he owns."
"8357","8352 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Safwan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: While the Messenger of Allah was traveling with his companions, he heard a man curse his she-camel, and said: Where is the one who cursed his she-camel? Hold her back, for you have been answered."
"8358","8353 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Safwan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise is a tree in whose shade a rider travels a hundred years; recite if you wish: (And extended shade)."
"8359","8354 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of uninterrupted fasting. They said: O Messenger of Allah, you fast uninterruptedly. He said: I am not like you; I spend the night with my Lord feeding me and giving me drink."
"8360","8355 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever bears arms against us is not of us."
"8361","8356 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the son of Adam with his wealth, family, and deeds is like a man who had three brothers, or three companions. One said: I am with you in your life; when you die, I am neither of you nor are you of me. Another said: I am with you; when you reach that tree, I am neither of you nor are you of me. And another said: I am with you, alive and dead."
"8362","8357 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Asim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best charity is what comes from surplus wealth; the upper hand is better than the lower hand; and begin with those you support."
"8363","8358 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Ibrahim was circumcised with an adze, after eighty years."
"8364","8359 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, he said: I heard my father mentioning from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever wrongfully takes - I think he said: A handspan of land - will be collared with it from seven earths."
"8365","8360 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, raising it, who said: Whoever takes a handspan of land without right will be collared with it from seven earths."
"8366","8361 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan who said: I heard my father narrating from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Three at whom Allah does not look: the lying ruler, the old adulterer, and the poor arrogant one."
"8367","8362 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us - I think he said: From Ibn Ajlan who said: I heard my father narrating from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the voice of a boy and shortened the prayer."
"8368","8363 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The lightest of the people of the Fire in punishment is one for whom two sandals of fire are made, from which his brain boils."
"8369","8364 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah. When they say it, they protect their blood and wealth except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah."
"8370","8365 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not combine my name and my kunyah; I am Abu al-Qasim; Allah gives and I distribute."
"8371","8366 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that one of you urinate in stagnant water, nor perform ghusl in it from janabah."
"8372","8367 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, and from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If a man peeps at his neighbor and he throws at his eye, there is nothing upon him."
"8373","8368 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Knowledge will be taken away, ignorance will appear, and harj will increase. They said: What is harj, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Fighting."
"8374","8369 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woman is like a rib; if you strive to straighten it you break it, and if you enjoy her you enjoy her while there is crookedness in her."
"8375","8370 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id and Abu Asim narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."
"8376","8371 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya, Safwan, and Abu Asim narrated to us, they said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah, Blessed and Exalted, created creation, He wrote with His hand upon Himself: My mercy overcomes My anger."
"8377","8372 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We have not made peace with them since we warred with them; whoever leaves any of them out of fear is not of us - meaning snakes."
"8378","8373 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, he said: I heard my father narrating from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My eyes sleep while my heart does not sleep."
"8379","8374 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya and Safwan narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever among you believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him honor his guest; whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not harm his neighbor; and whoever among you believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or remain silent."
"8380","8375 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghassan narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Amir ibn al-Akwa': Take from your little songs. He said - I think: And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Ibn Ajlan except Ibn Uyaynah, nor from him except Abu Ghassan. [The report as preserved here is brief/garbled; the matn ends at the quoted phrase.]"
"8381","8376 - Ibrahim ibn Harb al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Hamzah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no god but Allah keeps repelling from its sayers: its sayers do not care what befalls them in their religion so long as their world is safe for them; but when its sayers no longer care what befalls them in their religion for the safety of their world, and they say: There is no god but Allah, it will be said to them: You have lied."
"8382","8377 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Ajlan, freedman of al-Mushma'ill, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I see those behind me as I see those before me; straighten your rows, and perfect your bowing and prostration."
"8383","8378 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Ajlan, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was asked about riding sacrificial camels. He said: Ride it. He said: It is a sacrificial animal. He said: Ride it, woe to you - or: woe unto you."
"8384","8379 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Ajlan, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the slave whom the heat of the Fire befalls - I think he said: Then call him; if he refuses, feed him into his hand; and when you strike them, do not strike their faces."
"8385","8380 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Ajlan, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile while fasting; if someone reviles you, say: I am fasting. By the One in whose hand is my soul, the changed breath of the fasting person's mouth is sweeter to Allah than the scent of musk."
"8386","8381 - Amr narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Ajlan, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Men who do not attend the last Isha will surely stop, or I will burn their houses - or he said: Around their houses - with bundles of firewood."
"8387","8382 - al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever stands from his seat, or from a gathering, then returns, he has most right to it."
"8388","8383 - al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it. We do not know this hadith narrated from Ibn Ajlan except from this angle, and we hear it only from al-Hasan ibn Qaza'ah from Humayd, combining them both."
"8389","8384 - al-Husayn ibn Ali al-Hannat narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: al-Nu'man, meaning Ibn Abd al-Salam, narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The slave has his food and clothing, and he is not tasked of work except what he can bear. We do not know that Malik narrated as musnad from Ibn Ajlan except this hadith."
"8390","8385 - Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, he said: Ma'di ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A man's lineage is his wealth, and his nobility is his piety - or he said: Lineage is wealth, and nobility is piety."
"8391","8386 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Ma'di ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan informed us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). [No matn is stated in this row beyond the chain.]"
"8392","8387 - Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sawwaf narrated to us, he said: Ma'di ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever attends a funeral among its family has a qirat; if he follows it, he has a qirat; if he prays over it, he has a qirat; and if he waits until it is buried, he has a qirat. We do not know anyone who narrated this hadith except Ma'di from Ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah."
"8393","Hilal, father of Muhammad ibn Hilal, from Abu Hurayrah. 8388 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hilal narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Congregational prayer is better than the prayer of the lone person by twenty-five degrees."
"8394","8389 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hilal narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: It is not lawful for a believer to desert a believer for more than three days."
"8395","8390 - Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hilal narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand elsewhere among the mosques except the Sacred Mosque."
"8396","8391 - Rizqullah ibn Musa and Sa'id ibn Bahr al-Qaratisiyy narrated to us, they said: Ma'n ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hilal narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he went out, we would stand for him until he entered his house. Muhammad ibn Hilal is a Madinan; we do not know anyone who narrated from his father other than him, so he is well-known, and his father is known through his son."
"8397","Nafi', freedman of Abdullah ibn Umar, from Abu Hurayrah. 8392 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi', from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When Allah loves a servant, He calls Jibril: Allah, Blessed and Exalted, loves so-and-so, so love him. He said: So Jibril loves him. He said: Then Jibril calls among the people of heaven: Allah loves so-and-so, so love him. He said: So the people of heaven love him; then acceptance is placed for him on earth. We do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Nafi', from Abu Hurayrah, except Musa ibn Uqbah, nor anyone who narrated it from Musa except Ibn Jurayj."
"8398","8393 - al-Abbas ibn Abdillah al-Bakasani narrated to us, he said: Yasarah ibn Safwan narrated to us, he said: Abu Ma'shar narrated to us, from Nafi', from Abu Hurayrah, who said: Wealth was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: There is no owner of gold or silver who did not pay its due except there will be brought forth for him upon the amplest of what it was, spread out for him on a smooth plain, heated upon it in the fire of Hell, branding his forehead and brow; whenever it cools, it is reheated upon him again, until he sees his path either to Paradise or to the Fire. And there is no owner of camels who did not pay its due - and among its due is milking them on the day of watering - except they are gathered for him at their amplest, trampling him with their hooves; whenever the first of them passes, the last returns upon him, until judgment is passed between people, or he sees his path."
"8399","Ibn Abi Dhu'bab, from Abu Hurayrah. 8394 - Ubayd ibn Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Ibn Abi Dhu'bab, from Abu Hurayrah who said: A man among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a mountain pass with water and was pleased by its pleasantness, saying: If only I secluded myself from people and stayed in this pass - but I will not do it until I seek permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not do it; the standing of one of you in the path of Allah is better for him than his staying in his house for sixty years - or so many years; whoever fights in the path of Allah for the time between two milkings of a camel, Paradise becomes due for him."
"8400","8395 - Ibrahim ibn Ziyad al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Abi Dhu'bab, from his uncle, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you breathe into the vessel when drinking from it; rather, when he wants to breathe, let him move it away, then breathe."
